: null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q27", "text": "Clownfish live among sea anemones' tentacles. Clownfish protect sea anemones by chasing away attackers. In turn, sea anemones protect Clownfish from predators. This type of symbiosis is", "options": ["parasitism.", "commensalism.", "mutualism.", "predation.", "speciation."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q30", "text": "The first carnivore in the food chain is", "options": ["one step from the primary producer.", "two steps from the primary producer.", "three steps from the primary producer.", "two steps from the herbivore.", "three steps from the herbivore."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q48", "text": "Which is NOT true about Tundra?\nI. It includes wide variety of animal species.\nII. It is called permafrost.\nIII. It is dominated by conifers.\nIV. It is located in far northern parts of North America, Europe, and Asia.", "options": ["I only", "III only", "I and III", "II and IV", "I, III and IV"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q64", "text": "The following graph shows the changes in the total volume of ice in Antarctica since 1994.Based on the data in the above graph, the greatest volume of ice was lost", "options": ["between 1994 and 2000.", "between 2002 and 2006.", "between 2008 and 2016.", "between 2002 and 2016.", "between 1994 and 2016."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 340\" width=\"100%\" height=\"340\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\