 than that of species B.", "It is mutualism since the population size of species A increased more than that of species B.", "It is mutualism since the population size of both species A and B increased.", "It is commensalism since the population size of species A increased more than that of species B."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph TD\n    subgraph Graph1 [\"Graph 1: Species Introduced\"]\n        A1[\"Species A: Population rises\"]\n        B1[\"Species B: Population rises\"]\n        A1 & B1 --> Mutualism[\"Both species benefit -> Mutualism\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Graph2 [\"Graph 2: Species Introduced\"]\n        A2[\"Species A: Stays unchanged / horizontal\"]\n        B2[\"Species B: Population rises\"]\n        A2 & B2 --> Commensalism[\"One benefits, one unaffected -> Commensalism\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q32", "text": "(Graphs) What conclusion can be derived concerning the type of symbiosis shown in graph 2?", "options": ["It is commensalism since the population size of species A remained constant while that of species B increased.", "It is parasitism since the population size of species A remained constant while that of species B increased.", "It is mutualism since the population size of species A remained constant while that of species B increased.", "It is mutualism since the population size of species A is greater than that of species B.", "It is parasitism since the population size of species A is greater than that of species B."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph TD\n    subgraph Graph1 [\"Graph 1: Species Introduced\"]\n        A1[\"Species A: Population rises\"]\n        B1[\"Species B: Population rises\"]\n        A1 & B1 --> Mutualism[\"Both species benefit -> Mutualism\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Graph2 [\"Graph 2: Species Introduced\"]\n        A2[\"Species A: Stays unchanged / horizontal\"]\n        B2[\"Species B: Population rises\"]\n        A2 & B2 --> Commensalism[\"One benefits, one unaffected -> Commensalism\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q42", "text": "A group of living things belonging to the same species and living in the same area is defined as a", "options": ["species", "population", "community", "ecosystem", "biome"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q43", "text": "In a food chain, the energy received by a 2ⁿᵈ level consumer is 17 calories. What is the amount of energy released by the producer?", "options": ["0.17 calories", "1.7 calories", "17 calories", "170 calories", "1700 calories"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q46", "text": "The movement of individuals into a new habitat in search of resources is called", "options": ["immigration", "emigration", "logistic growth", "exponential growth", "birth rate"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q51", "text": "(Graph) What conclusion can be derived from the information presented in the above graph? (CO₂ & global temperature)", "options": ["The amount of CO₂ started to increase sharply starting in 1900, thus causing an increase in the global temperature from around 57.0°F to 58.5°F.", "The amount of CO₂ started to increase sharply starting in 1900, thus causing a decrease in the global temperature from around 58.5°F to 57.0°F.", "The amount of CO₂ started to increase sharply starting in 1980, thus causing an increase in the global temperature from around 57.5°F to 58.5°F.", "The amount of CO₂ started to increase sharply starting in 1980, thus causing a decrease in the global temperature from 58.5°F to 57.5°F.", "The amount of CO₂ started to increase sharply starting in 1920, thus causing an increase in the global temperature from 57.0°F to 58.5°F."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    P1[\"1880-1980:<br>Gradual CO2 increase, steady temp\"] --> P2[\"Starting in 1980:<br>Sharp CO2 surge (>380 ppm)\"]\n    P2 --> Warming[\"Global temp rises sharply: 57.5°F -> 58.5°F\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q52", "text": "In a food chain, the energy produced by the plants is 25,000 kcal/m²/year. What is the amount of energy captured by the 2ⁿᵈ level consumer?", "options": ["2.5 kcal/m²/year", "25 kcal/m²/year", "250 kcal/m²/year", "2500 kcal/m²/year", "25000 kcal/m²/year"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q53", "text": "What is the amount of energy captured by the 4ᵗʰ level consumer?", "options": ["2.5 kcal/m²/year", "25 kcal/m²/year", "250 kcal/m²/year", "2500 kcal/m²/year", "25000 kcal/m²/year"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q54", "text": "Both cheetahs and lions hunt the same prey such as antelope. If cheetahs and lions live in the same area, one or both will have less food. This is an example of", "options": ["commensalism", "predator-prey relationship", "competition", "herbivory", "mutualism"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q57", "text": "(Graphs) We can conclude that this is an example of (P. aurelia and P. caudatum growth)", "options": ["competition", "predation", "parasitism", "commensalism", "mutualism"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"20\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Both species grown together</text>\n  