h-altitude meadows of California Sierra Nevada. Which of the following terms best describes an interbreeding group of Sierra sulphur butterflies?", "options": ["Biome", "Community", "Ecosystem", "Population"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q85", "text": "When sea otter was removed from this food chain, the population of sea urchins increased dramatically. The removal of sea otters from food chain could have contributed to the increase in population of sea urchins by:", "options": ["Decreasing competition between sea otters and sea urchins for kelp", "Increasing competition between sea otters and sea urchins for kelp", "Decreasing predation pressure by sea otters, allowing more sea urchins to survive longer to produce more offspring", "Increasing predation pressure by sea otters, preventing most of the sea urchins from surviving to produce offspring"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 300\" width=\"420\" height=\"300\" style=\"background:#e0f2fe; font-family:sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0369a1\">Simple Marine Food Chain</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60, 210)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#15803d\"/>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Giant Kelp</text>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#166534\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Producer)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60, 60)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#9333ea\"/>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sea Urchin</text>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"-10\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7e22ce\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Primary Consumer)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(260, 60)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sea Otter</text>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"-10\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#9a3412\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Secondary Consumer)</text>\n  </g>\n  <line x1=\"115\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"115\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"115,105 110,118 120,118\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/>\n  <line x1=\"170\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"260,82 247,77 247,87\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q24", "text": "A shark feeding on a fish, a fox feeding on a rabbit, and a bird feeding on an insect are all examples of which of the following types of interaction?", "options": ["Competition", "Mutualism", "Herbivory", "Predation"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q28", "text": "Seven species of Anolis lizards successfully coexist in the same habitat and feed on insects and other arthropods. Which of the following statements best explains their ability to coexist in the same habitat?", "options": ["The species have different reproductive cycles", "Individuals fail to identify others as belonging to different species", "High levels of competition exist between members of the 7 species", "Each species occupies a distinct niche"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q39", "text": "In a simple food chain, hawks eat insectivorous birds, insectivorous birds eat insects, and insects eat leaves on trees. The relative number of each of these 4 types of organisms present at each trophic level in this food chain is best represented by which of the following diagrams?", "options": ["Diagram A (Inverted pyramid base)", "Diagram B (Spindle-shaped pyramid)", "Diagram C (Upright pyramid)", "Diagram D (Hourglass pyramid)"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 240\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <g transform=\"translate(10, 20)\">\n    <text x=\"60\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text>\n    <rect x=\"52\" y=\"30\" width=\"16\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"35\" y=\"60\" width=\"50\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"15\" y=\"90\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"30\" y=\"120\" width=\"60\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(160, 20)\">\n    <text x=\"60\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">B</text>\n    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"30\" width=\"14\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"42\" y=\"60\" width=\"36\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"25\" y=\"90\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"5\" y=\"120\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(310, 20)\">\n    <text x=\"60\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">C</text>\n    <rect x=\"53\" y=\"30\" width=\"14\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"60\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"25\" y=\"90\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"5\" y=\"120\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(460, 20)\">\n    <text x=\"60\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text>\n    <rect x=\"52\" y=\"30\" width=\"16\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"45\" y=\"60\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"35\" y=\"90\" width=\"50\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"120\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#475569\">Levels (bottom to top): Trees → Insects → Insectivorous Birds → Hawks</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q42", "text": "Based on the Antarctic Food Web, which are two organisms that compete for the same food?", "options": ["Krill and herbivorous zooplankton", "Krill and sperm whale", "Herbivorous zooplankton and seals", "Herbivorous zooplankton and baleen whales"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 420\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 1 L 8 5 L 0 9 z\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/>\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"220\" y=\"370\" width=\"160\" height=\"35\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ecfdf5\" stroke=\"#059669\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"392\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#065f46\">Phytoplankton</text>\n  <r