\" y=\"30\" width=\"130\" height=\"32\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fef2f2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\"/>\n  <text x=\"285\" y=\"51\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#991b1b\">Smaller Toothed Whales</text>\n  <line x1=\"260\" y1=\"370\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"325\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"340\" y1=\"370\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"325\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"145\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"145\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"145\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"265\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"445\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"460\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"445\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"290\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"145\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"460\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"145\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"220\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q52", "text": "Tiny single-celled algae called zooxanthellae live inside the bodies of reef-building corals. Through photosynthesis, zooxanthellae provide corals with carbohydrates, oxygen, and the proper pH to build coral skeletons. The corals provide the zooxanthellae with a safe environment, a source of carbon dioxide, and nutrients. What type of interaction is this?", "options": ["Commensalism", "Mutualism", "Competition", "Parasitism"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q63", "text": "A region in Australia has an average annual temperature of 25°C and an average annual precipitation of 385 cm. According to this diagram, which type of biome is most likely found in this region?", "options": ["Temperate deciduous forest", "Tropical rain forest", "Temperate rain forest", "Tropical seasonal forest"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 380\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"520\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#0f172a\" rx=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"320\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">Average Annual Temperature (°C)</text>\n  <text x=\"25\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 25 180)\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">Annual Precipitation (cm)</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">-10</text>\n  <text x=\"172\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">0</text>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">10</text>\n  <text x=\"377\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">20</text>\n  <text x=\"480\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">30</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">0</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">100</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">200</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">300</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">400</text>\n  <polygon points=\"380,180 430,40 480,140 480,240 380,220\" fill=\"#15803d\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"440\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tropical Rainforest</text>\n  <polygon points=\"275,220 380,180 380,250 275,270\" fill=\"#0284c7\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"10\">Temperate Rainforest</text>\n  <circle cx=\"430\" cy=\"50\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#ef4444\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"415\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fca5a5\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">(25°C, 385 cm)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q66", "text": "Many orchids live in tropical rain forests high in tree branches. They receive water and nutrients that fall from trees' upper leaves. However, their roots don't connect to the trees and they provide no benefit to the trees. What kind of ecological interaction is this?", "options": ["Commensalism", "Mutualism", "Competition", "Parasitism"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q71", "text": "Which of the following best describes an ecological community?", "options": ["A group of populations of different species that occupy the same geographical region", "A group of populations of different species and their abiotic environment", "A group of organisms of the same species living in the same geographical environment", "A particular place in which a specific species lives"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q76", "text": "A new island is formed by a volcanic eruption. Soil gradually develops on this new island, allowing grasses and other herbaceous plants to grow. These grasses and other herbaceous plants are gradually replaced by woody shrubs that are then replaced by trees. This change in community composition over time is best described as which of the following?", "options": ["Succession", "Reproductive isolation", "Speciation", "Geographic isolation"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q17", "text": "Tiny single-celled algae called zooxanthellae live inside the bodies of reef-building corals. Through photosynthesis, zooxanthellae provide corals with carbohydrates, oxygen, and the proper pH to build coral skeletons. The corals provide the zooxanthellae with a protected environment, a source of carbon dioxide, and nutrients. What type of interaction is this?", "options": ["Commensalism", "Competition", "Mutualism", "Parasitism"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q25", "text": "Hydrothermal vents are found on the ocean floor where hot, mineral-rich water escapes from cracks in Earth's crust. Bacteria near the vents do not require sunlight. Instead, they get energy by oxidizing hydrogen sulfide. Clams, shrimp, and giant tube worms consume these bacteria. These animals, in turn, are consumed by larger animals. Removing which of the following components from a hydrothermal vent ecosystem would most likely impose the greatest limit on ecosystem productivity?", "options": ["Clams and shrimp", "Hydrogen sulfide", "Larger animals", "Sunlight"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q30", "text": "According to this diagram, which type of biome is most likely found in this region? (Avg temp 25°C, avg precip 285 cm)", "options": ["Temperate deciduous forest", "Temperate rain forest", "Tropical rain forest", "Tropical seasonal forest"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 650 520\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"650\" height=\"520\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#E2E8F0\" 