"est-old-2-q6", "text": "The wings of the bird and wings of the bee are ________, while the arms of the monkey and the flippers of the whale are ________", "options": ["homologous structures, analogous structures", "analogous structures, vestigial structures", "analogous structures, homologous structures", "homologous structures, vestigial structures", "vestigial structures, homologous structures"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q15", "text": "Speciation is the result ofI. random mating.II. temporal isolation.III. geographic isolation.IV. no mutation in the population.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "I and IV", "II and III", "I, II and III"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q18", "text": "Which statement is true about evidence of evolution?\nI. Closely related organisms go through similar stages in their embryonic development.\nII. Closely related aerobic organisms have cytochrome c with an identical chain of amino acids.\nIII. Organisms that have common ancestors have common biochemical pathways.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "I and II", "II and III", "I, II and III"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q47", "text": "Yellow grasshoppers are easily caught by predators, whereas green grasshoppers hide from predators by camouflage. This is called", "options": ["adaptation.", "temporal isolation.", "survival of the fittest.", "artificial selection.", "speciation."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q53", "text": "A genetic condition is controlled by 2 alleles: dominant \"S\" and recessive \"s\". This genetic condition only affects homozygous recessive individuals. In a population of size 10,000, there are 36 affected individuals.The frequency of q is", "options": ["94%.", "6%.", "0.36%.", "88.36%.", "11.28%."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q54", "text": "The frequency of p is", "options": ["6%.", "0.36%.", "11.28%.", "94%.", "88.36%."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q55", "text": "The frequency of SS (homozygous dominant) is", "options": ["0.36%.", "88.36%.", "94%.", "6%.", "11.28%."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q56", "text": "The frequency of ss (homozygous recessive) is", "options": ["88.36%.", "11.28%.", "94%.", "6%.", "0.36%."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q57", "text": "The frequency of Ss (hybrid) is", "options": ["6%.", "0.36%.", "88.36%.", "11.28%.", "94%."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q60", "text": "The heterotroph hypothesis states that", "options": ["the first cells on Earth were anaerobic heterotrophic prokaryotes.", "the first cells on Earth were aerobic heterotrophic prokaryotes.", "the first cells on Earth were anaerobic heterotrophic eukaryotes.", "the first cells on Earth were aerobic autotrophic prokaryotes.", "the first cells on Earth were aerobic autotrophic eukaryotes."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-3-q3", "text": "Once the Earth was formed, its atmosphere largely consisted of:I. O2​II. CH4​III. NH3​IV. H2​OV. N2​", "options": ["I and IV", "I, II, and IV", "I, IV, and V", "I, II, III, and IV", "II, III, IV, and V"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-3-q14", "text": "A farmer's use of the cows that produce large amounts of milk for breeding is an example of", "options": ["artificial selection.", "natural selection.", "extinction.", "adaptation.", "genetic drift."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-3-q18", "text": "Cytochrome c is a small protein involved in cellular respiration. Many studies were done in attempt to study the amino acids that form cytochrome c in chimpanzees and in other organisms. The following table shows the number of amino acids that are different from those in chimpanzees with cytochrome c.  We can conclude from the above study that", "options": ["yeast probably shares the most common ancestor with the chimpanzee.", "the moth probably shares the most common ancestor with the chimpanzee.", "the dog probably shares the most common ancestor with the chimpanzee.", "the penguin probably shares the most common ancestor with the chimpanzee.", "the moth and yeast probably share the most common ancestor with the chimpanzee."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"490\" height=\"175\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"132\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"132\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"515\" y2=\"164\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"170\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0f172a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <t