st-old-5-q4", "text": "What is the frequency of the allele for red coat color in the foxes?", "options": ["0.09", "0.03", "0.3", "0.55", "0.9"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q5", "text": "In this population of foxes, what percentage is hybrid red?", "options": ["7%", "50%", "60%", "81%", "91%"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q6", "text": "If the climate were to change so that snow covered the ground much of the time, what change in the population of foxes would you expect?", "options": ["The frequency of white allele would increase.", "The frequency of white allele would decrease.", "The frequency of red allele would increase.", "The population of foxes would decrease and then increase.", "The population of foxes would increase and then decrease."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q15", "text": "Which of the following is LEAST likely to result in speciation?", "options": ["random mating among members of a large population of a species", "occurrence of hybridization between individuals from two different species", "development of different mating behavior by some members of a species", "emigration to a specialized microenvironment by some members of a species", "formation of a physical barrier that blocks gene flow between members of a species"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q18", "text": "Inheritance of acquired traits", "options": ["Charles Darwin", "Lamarck", "Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge", "Oparin and Haldane", "Hardy-Weinberg"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q19", "text": "Use and disuse", "options": ["Charles Darwin", "Lamarck", "Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge", "Oparin and Haldane", "Hardy-Weinberg"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q20", "text": "Theory of punctuated equilibrium", "options": ["Charles Darwin", "Lamarck", "Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge", "Oparin and Haldane", "Hardy-Weinberg"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q21", "text": "Populations tend to overpopulate", "options": ["Charles Darwin", "Lamarck", "Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge", "Oparin and Haldane", "Hardy-Weinberg"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q22", "text": "Hypothesized that under conditions that existed in early Earth, organic molecules could form", "options": ["Charles Darwin", "Lamarck", "Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge", "Oparin and Haldane", "Hardy-Weinberg"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q23", "text": "Survival of the fittest", "options": ["Charles Darwin", "Lamarck", "Stephen J. Gould and Niles Eldridge", "Oparin and Haldane", "Hardy-Weinberg"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q29", "text": "Wildebeests separated from each other by a newly formed river are now separate species. This fact corresponds to", "options": ["divergent evolution.", "convergent evolution.", "coevolution.", "parallel evolution.", "genetic drift."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q37", "text": "Darwin discovered 14 species of finches on the Galapagos Islands that all evolved from one original species of finch. This is an example of", "options": ["geographic isolation.", "polyploidy.", "reproductive isolation.", "adaptive radiation.", "direc