 font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">'10</text>\n\n  <rect x=\"245\" y=\"88\" width=\"30\" height=\"62\" fill=\"#0275d8\"/>\n  <text x=\"260\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">'15</text>\n\n  <rect x=\"305\" y=\"79\" width=\"30\" height=\"71\" fill=\"#0275d8\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">'20</text>\n\n  <rect x=\"365\" y=\"69\" width=\"30\" height=\"81\" fill=\"#0275d8\"/>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">'25</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-3-q36", "text": "Homologous structures are", "options": ["similar anatomical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, but these structures serve different functions.", "similar anatomical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, and these structures serve similar functions.", "different anatomical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, and these structures serve completely different functions.", "different anatomical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, and these structures serve similar functions.", "structures that are inherited from common ancestors but have lost their original function."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q37", "text": "A type of natural selection where individuals near the center of the curve have higher fitness than individuals at both ends of the curve is called", "options": ["directional selection", "artificial selection", "disruptive selection", "stabilizing selection", "bottleneck effect"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q46", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. According to the Hardy Weinberg principle, the above probability of homozygote brown lentil is represented by", "options": ["p", "p²", "q", "q²", "pq"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q47", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. The allele frequency of dominant brown lentils is", "options": ["0.3", "0.245", "0.49", "0.7", "0.07"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q48", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. The allele frequency of recessive red lentils is", "options": ["0.51", "0.3", "0.03", "0.42", "0.755"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q49", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. The probability of individuals to be heterozygote is", "options": ["0.21", "0.088", "0.42", "0.044", "0.9"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q25", "text": "Body organs belonging to different organisms that perform similar functions but have different structures are known as", "options": ["analogous structures", "homologous structures", "vestigial organs", "acquired structures", "fossils"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q33", "text": "(Diagram) What conclusion can be drawn from the fossils presented? (Rock layers)", "options": ["Primates appeared before mammals, which in turn appeared before fish.", "Mammals appeared before fish, which in turn appeared before primates.", "Fish appeared before mammals, which in turn appeared before primates.", "Fish appeared before primates, which in turn appeared before mammals.", "Mammals appeared before primates, which in turn appeared before fish."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 350 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <!-- Top Layer -->\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"20\" width=\"290\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#d7ccc8\" stroke=\"#5d4037\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"175\" y=\"48\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Primates (Youngest)</text>\n\n  <!-- Middle Layer -->\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"65\" width=\"290\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#ffccbc\" stroke=\"#5d4037\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"175\" y=\"93\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mammals (Intermediate)</text>\n\n  <!-- Bottom Layer -->\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"110\" width=\"290\" height=\"45\" fill=\"#bcaaa4\" stroke=\"#5d4037\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"175\" y=\"138\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fish (Oldest)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q41", "text": "(Graph) What conclusion can be derived from the results presented in the above graph? (Beak size vs. survival)", "options": ["During the drought period, birds with larger beaks have a lower chance of survival.", "During the drought period, birds with larger beaks have a higher chance of survival.", "During the drought period, all beak-sized birds were able to survive.", "During the drought period, only the small beak-sized birds were able to survive.", "During the drought period, all birds were not able to survive despite their beak size."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"195\" y=\"172\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Beak Size (mm)</text>\n  <text x=\"-85\" y=\"18\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Surviving %</text>\n\n  <path d=\"M 60 148 Q 180 145 240 100 Q 280 60 320 25\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#d32f2f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"25\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#d32f2f\"/>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"20\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#d32f2f\" font-weight=\"bold\">High survival: 12-13 mm</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q44", "text": "Vestigial structures are", "options": ["similar physical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, but these structures serve completely different functions.", "similar physical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, and these structures serve similar functions.", "different physical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, and these structures serve completely different functions.", "different physical structures in organisms that share a common ancestor, but these structures serve similar functions.", "structures that are inherited from ancestors but have lost their original function."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q1", "text": "What term refers to features inherited from the same evolutionary origin but adapted to different functions?", "options": ["Homologous structures", "Analogous structures", "Cladogram", "Common ancestor", "Vestigial structures"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q2", "text": "What kind of diagram is used to represent evolutionary relationships based on shared characteristics?", "options": ["Homologous structures", "Analogous structures", "Cladogram", "Common ancestor", "Vestigial structures"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q3", "text": "What term refers to a species from which two or more species are believed to have evolved?", "options": ["Homologous structures", "Analogous structures", "Cladogram", "Common ancestor", "Vestigial structures"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q4", "text": "What structures have no current function but are remnants of features that were functional in ancestors?", "options": ["Homologous structures", "Analogous structures", "Cladogram", "Common ancestor", "Vestigial structures"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q5", "text": "What term describes features with similar functions that evolved independently in unrelated lineages?", "options": ["Homologous structures", "Analogous structures", "Cladogram", "Common ancestor", "Vestigial structures"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q11", "text": "(Cladogram) Which animals have vertebrae, a bony skeleton and four limbs but no amniotic eggs?", "options": ["Crocodiles and Birds", "Sharks", "Amphibians", "Ray-finned fish", "Primates, Rodents and Rabbits"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Root((Vertebrate Ancestor)) --> Sharks[\"Sharks (Cartilaginous)\"]\n    Root --> N1[\"Bony skeleton\"]\n    N1 --> RayFish[\"Ray-finned fish\"]\n    N1 --> N2[\"Four limbs\"]\n    N2 --> Amphibians[\"Amphibians\"]\n    N2 --> N3[\"Amniotic egg\"]\n    N3 --> N4[\"Hair\"]\n    N4 --> Mammals[\"Primates, Rodents & Rabbits\"]\n    N3 --> N5[\"Eggs with shells\"]\n    N5 --> Archosaurs[\"Crocodiles and Birds\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q12", "text": "(Cladogram) Which animals have vertebrae, a bony skeleton, four limbs, amniotic eggs and hair?", "options": ["Crocodiles and Birds", "Sharks", "Amphibians", "Ray-finned fish", "Primates, Rodents and Rabbits"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Root((Vertebrate Ancestor)) --> Sharks[\"Sharks (Cartilaginous)\"]\n    Root --> N1[\"Bony skeleton\"]\n    N1 --> RayFish[\"Ray-finned fish\"]\n    N1 --> N2[\"Four limbs\"]\n    N2 --> Amphibians[\"Amphibians\"]\n    N2 --> N3[\"Amniotic egg\"]\n    N3 --> N4[\"Hair\"]\n    N4 --> Mammals[\"Primates, Rodents & Rabbits\"]\n    N3 --> N5[\"Eggs with shells\"]\n    N5 --> Archosaurs[\"Crocodiles and Birds\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q13", "text": "(Cladogram) Which animals have vertebrae, a bony skeleton, four limbs, amniotic eggs and eggs with shells?", "options": ["Crocodiles and Birds", "Sharks", "Amphibians", "Ray-finned fish", "Primates, Rodents and Rabbits"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Root((Vertebrate Ancestor)) --> Sharks[\"Sharks (Cartilaginous)\"]\n    Root --> N1[\"Bony skeleton\"]\n    N1 --> RayFish[\"Ray-finned fish\"]\n    N1 --> N2[\"Four limbs\"]\n    N2 --> Amphibians[\"Amphibians\"]\n    N2 --> N3[\"Amniotic egg\"]\n    N3 --> N4[\"Hair\"]\n    N4 --> Mammals[\"Primates, Rodents & Rabbits\"]\n    N3 --> N5[\"Eggs with shells\"]\n    N5 --> Archosaurs[\"Crocodiles and Birds\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q14", "text": "(Cladogram) Which animals do not have a bony skeleton?", "options": ["Crocodiles and Birds", "Sharks", "Amphibians", "Ray-finned fish", "Primates, Rodents and Rabbits"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Root((Vertebrate Ancestor)) --> Sharks[\"Sharks (Cartilaginous)\"]\n    Root --> N1[\"Bony skeleton\"]\n    N1 --> RayFish[\"Ray-finned fish\"]\n    N1 --> N2[\"Four limbs\"]\n    N2 --> Amphibians[\"Amphibians\"]\n    N2 --> N3[\"Amniotic egg\"]\n    N3 --> N4[\"Hair\"]\n    N4 --> Mammals[\"Primates, Rodents & Rabbits\"]\n    N3 --> N5[\"Eggs with shells\"]\n    N5 --> Archosaurs[\"Crocodiles and Birds\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q15", "text": "(Cladogram) Which animals have vertebrae, a bony skeleton but no four limbs?", "options": ["Crocodiles and Birds", "Sharks", "Amphibians", "Ray-finned fish", "Primates, Rodents and Rabbits"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Root((Vertebrate Ancestor)) --> Sharks[\"Sharks (Cartilaginous)\"]\n    Root --> N1[\"Bony skeleton\"]\n    N1 --> RayFish[\"Ray-finned fish\"]\n    N1 --> N2[\"Four limbs\"]\n    N2 --> Amphibians[\"Amphibians\"]\n    N2 --> N3[\"Amniotic egg\"]\n    N3 --> N4[\"Hair\"]\n    N4 --> Mammals[\"Primates, Rodents & Rabbits\"]\n    N3 --> N5[\"Eggs with shells\"]\n    N5 --> Archosaurs[\"Crocodiles and Birds\"]\n"}, {"id": "act-1-q5", "text": "Scientists found fossils of an animal in different continents that are now separated, what is the reason?", "options": ["The animal roamed around in all continents that were once joined.", "Animal migrates.", "Someone spread the fossils", "Unknown"], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 650 400\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"background:#f8fafc; font-family:system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\">\n  <defs>\n    <filter id=\"plate-shadow\" x=\"-10%\" y=\"-10%\" width=\"120%\" height=\"120%\">\n      <feDropShadow dx=\"1\" dy=\"2\" stdDeviation=\"2\" flood-opacity=\"0.15\" />\n    </filter>\n  </defs>\n\n  <text x=\"325\" y=\"35\" text