ght=\"600\" fill=\"#c2410c\">Orange band: Continuous discovery zone of identical animal fossils</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-1-q15", "text": "Birds with large beaks and birds with small beaks are widespread in the environment, while medium beaks are in intermediate amounts. Type of natural selection:", "options": ["Disruptive selection.", "Directional selection.", "Stabilizing selection.", "Convergent selection."], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q16", "text": "Organism A can only survive, organism B survive and reproduce, organism C have long life span, organism D is the strongest. Which of the following is most fit according to Darwin?", "options": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q18", "text": "Less genetic variation in population cause:", "options": ["Less chances of survival.", "More chances of survival.", "More adaptation.", "No change."], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q57", "text": "The misuse of antibiotics contributes to the spread of resistant strains of bacteria. The misuse of antibiotics can result in:", "options": ["The transfer of nuclei from bacteria to viruses.", "The transfer of nuclei from viruses to bacteria.", "A decrease in the frequency of antibiotic resistance genes in a population of bacteria.", "An increase in the frequency of antibiotic resistance allele in a population of bacteria."], "answer": 3, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q82", "text": "We shall consider theory of endosymbiosis to be true because these organelles contain", "options": ["ATP", "DNA", "Ribosome", "Starch"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q84", "text": "What is the scientific meaning of biological evolution?", "options": ["The development of an organism during its lifetime", "The change in inherited traits over successive generations in population of species", "The increase in the concentration of harmful chemicals in each trophic level.", "The use of living organisms to control pests"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q96", "text": "Which of the following is true regarding the similarities between Fins of shark and fins of dolphin?", "options": ["Evidence of common ancestors", "Evidence of convergent evolution", "Share homologous structures", "Share vestigial structures"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q100", "text": "Scientists have observed that the gene that codes for RNA polymerase is present in all living species and that there are few differences between species in the DNA sequence that code for RNA polymerase. Which of the following statements provides the most likely explanation for the observation?", "options": ["Similarities in RNA polymerase resulted from non-random mating.", "The common ancestor of all organisms had RNA polymerase", "Convergent evolution led to similarities in RNA polymerase.", "The RNA polymerase gene does not mutate."], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q7", "text": "Which of the following share the most recent common ancestor", "options": ["A & B", "B & C", "A & C", "A, B and C"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 450 250\" width=\"100%\" height=\"250\">\n  <rect width=\"450\"