": "act-3-q56", "text": "what would be change evolution occur?", "options": ["population size", "allele frequency.", "type of species.", "habitat that organisms live in."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q3", "text": "While traveling on HMS Beagle, Charles Darwin made observations that would later provide information about:", "options": ["evidence that earth is less than 20,000 years old", "an original system of classified plants and animals that is still used to day", "direct biochemical evidence that genes are passed from parents to offspring", "information regarding the geographical distribution of organisms"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q5", "text": "Dorsal lines of dolphins and sharks appear similar in shape. Does this type of similarity indicate that the 2 species came from same common ancestor?", "options": ["no, they may evolve independently in dolphin and shark because the exist in same environment", "no, they differently shaped dorsal lines would indicate the 2 species inherited the lines from a common ancestor", "yes, their similarity in structure indicates the two species have a common ancestor", "yes, the two species that exist in similar environment must have inherited the trait from a common ancestor"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q6", "text": "What must occur for two species to be considered different species? I. they should be geographically isolated. II. they should be reproductively isolated. III. They should share same ecological niche.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "I and II only", "I, II, III"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q31", "text": "Which of the following share same common ancestor?", "options": ["A and B", "A and C", "A, B, and C", "None of them"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 240\" width=\"320\" height=\"240\" style=\"background:#fff; font-family:sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\">Phylogenetic Tree</text>\n  <line x1=\"160\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n  <text x=\"130\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text>\n  <text x=\"240\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C</text>\n  <circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"150\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#dc2626\">Common Ancestor (A, B, C)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-4-q32", "text": "Which of the following statements is true about fossils and rocks that fossils are found in?", "options": ["all fossils are older than the layers they found in", "all fossils are younger than the layers they found in", "older fossils are found in deeper layers of rocks, and younger fossils are found in new layers of rocks", "younger fossils are found deeper layers of rocks, and older fossils are found in new rock layers"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q35", "text": "After a forest has been destroyed by fire, the population pf plants consisted of small plants and mosses. Why tall trees are not a part of the plant population?", "options": ["small plant and mosses evolved from trees", "trees evolved from small plants and mosses", "trees are better in adapting the biotic and abiotic factors in environment post fire", "small plants and mosses are better in adapting the biotic and abiotic factors in environment post fire"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q37", "text": "DDT is an insecticide used to get rid of insects related diseases in 1890. At first exposure, 99% of insects are died. What will happen during next exposure to DDT?", "options": ["less than 1% will survive, due to decrease frequency of mutant resistant allele", "less than 1% will survive due to increase frequency of mutant resistant alleles", "more than 1% will survive because decrease frequency of mutant resistant alleles", "more than 1% will survive due to increase the frequency of mutant resistant allele"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q39", "text": "Two populations of same species are separated by canyon, and no organism move between two populations. These two populations will be:", "options": ["similar, because no organisms moved between two population", "dissimilar, because no organisms moved between two population", "similar, because organisms moved between two population", "dissimilar, because organisms moved between two population"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q45", "text": "DDT is an insecticide used to get rid of malaria. At first exposure, most of the paramecium died leaving few amount of paramecium. What is the type of natural selection here?", "options": ["directional selection", "stabilising selection", "disruptive selection", "diversifying selection"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q52", "text": "In an isolated population of sea lions, only 1 allele (allele L) of a particular gene was present. Was this rapid decrease in frequency of allele L more likely the result of gene glow or mutation?", "options": ["Gene flow, a spontaneous change in the DNA that codes for the gene gave rise to a different allele immediately after the new sea lions", "Gene flow, a different allele of the gene was introduced into this population by the new sea lions", "Mutation, a spontaneous change in the DNA that codes for this gene gave rise to a different allele immediately after the new sea lions were introduced", "Mutation, a different allele of the gene was introduced into the population by the new sea lions"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q58", "text": "Suppose that two groups of warblers population become geographically isolated. Over time the two populations of warblers become different species. Which of the following statements about these two populations is most likely correct?", "options": ["Population A did not evolve", "Population B did not evolve", "There was very little gene flow. If any, between populations A and B", "There was not any genetic divergence between populations A and B"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q36", "text": "While on the HMS Beagle, Charles Darwin made a stop at the Galapagos Islands. He observed that on islands with tortoise populations, prickly pear cactus fruits grew far above the ground. On islands without tortoise populations, prickly pear cactus fruits grew on or near the ground. These observations led Darwin to conclude that the tortoises acted as agents of selection on the prickly pear cacti by feeding on:", "options": ["Fruits from other species in the area", "Prickly pear cactus fruits growing anywhere on the cacti", "Prickly pear cactus fruits growing high above the ground only", "Prickly pear cactus fruits growing on or near the ground only"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q37", "text": "Fossils of the land-dwelling mammal-like reptile Lystrosaurus (millions of years old) have been found in Africa, India, Madagascar, and Antarctica. This map shows these locations on Earth. Which of the following statements provides the most likely explanation for the existence of Lystrosaurus in all 4 areas?", "options": ["Lystrosaurus bones drifted through the oceans and fossilized when they landed in continental sedimentary rocks", "Lystrosaurus swam between continents and survived the extreme temperature of Antarctica", "Lystrosaurus evolved on each continent independently and then went extinct", "Lystrosaurus lived and walked on these lands when they were once connected as one land mass"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 650 340\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"650\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"325\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"300\" ry=\"150\" fill=\"#e0f2fe\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M120,60 Q180,50 210,90 Q220,130 190,145 Q160,140 140,110 Z\" fill=\"#22c55e\" stroke=\"#15803d\"/>\n  <path d=\"M185,155 Q230,175 220,230 Q200,270 175,250 Q165,190 185,155 Z\" fill=\"#16a34a\" stroke=\"#15803d\"/>\n  <path d=\"M300,70 Q450,50 540,90 Q550,150 480,165 Q420,130 360,130 Q310,100 300,70 Z\" fill=\"#ea580c\" stroke=\"#c2410c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M290,120 Q365,120 375,170 Q370,225 330,245 Q295,200 290,120 Z\" fill=\"#eab308\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/>\n  <path d=\"M480,200 Q540,195 545,230 Q515,250 475,235 Z\" fill=\"#db2777\" stroke=\"#be185d\"/>\n  <path d=\"M160,290 Q325,270 490,290 Q400,315 250,315 Z\" fil