xperiences through the course of its lifetime", "A change in the proportions of inherited traits within a population occurring over successive generations", "A means by which random chance blends the characteristics an organism inherits from its parents following fertilization"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q68", "text": "The food source for a population of black-bellied seedcrackers consists of seeds that tend to have either large or small sizes. Very few seedcrackers have medium-sized beaks. Hard seeds can be readily eaten only by birds with large beaks; soft seeds can be readily eaten only by birds with small beaks. Based on this information, is the population of seedcrackers more likely influenced by directional selection or by disruptive selection?", "options": ["Directional; this type of selection favors the intermediate form of a trait", "Directional; this type of selection favors the 2 extreme forms of a trait", "Disruptive; this type of selection favors the intermediate form of a trait", "Disruptive; this type of selection favors the 2 extreme forms of a trait"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q79", "text": "A scientist observes four female gray wolves, each from a different pack: Female 1 has the thickest fur; Female 2 produces the most pups that survive to reproduce; Female 3 has the most relatives in her pack; Female 4 survives the longest. Based on Darwin's theory of natural selection, which female has the highest biological fitness?", "options": ["Female 1", "Female 3", "Female 2", "Female 4"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q80", "text": "Scientists often use the amino acid sequences of hemoglobin polypeptides to determine evolutionary relationships between organisms. The number of differences in the amino 