, "options": ["homozygous.", "homologous.", "heterozygous.", "non-homologous.", "true breeding."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q12", "text": "Traits controlled by more than one gene are", "options": ["codominant.", "incomplete dominant.", "dominant.", "multiple alleles.", "polygenic."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q14", "text": "After mating a black guinea pig and a white guinea pig, all offspring obtained were black. Which conclusion can be drawn from this cross?", "options": ["This trait is a single gene trait.", "This trait is a polygenic trait.", "This is a sex linked trait.", "This is codominant inheritance.", "This is intermediate dominant inheritance."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q28", "text": "Upon crossing a male rabbit having Bb genotype with a female rabbit having Bb genotype, the offspring obtained have genotypes with ratios of 2/3 Bb and 1/3 bb (it is a case of dominance inheritance with B as the dominant allele and b as the recessive allele). What can you conclude from this cross?", "options": ["Allele b is lethal allele.", "Allele B is lethal allele.", "Presence of allele B with allele b is lethal.", "Both alleles B and b are lethal.", "Individuals with pure genotypes do not survive."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q38", "text": "A plant having genotype TT is crossed with another plant having genotype Tt (T is the symbol of the dominant allele, and t is the symbol of the recessive allele). Which statement is true concerning the offspring that result from this cross?", "options": ["All offspring will have the dominant character as a phenotype.", "All offspring will have the recessive character as a phenotype.", "7