f the digestion occurs in the small intestine.", "Yes, since the food is predigested.", "No, since absorption of food occurs in the small intestine.", "Yes, since digestion of food ends in the stomach.", "Yes, since absorption of food occurs in the large intestine."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q61", "text": "A study was done in order to monitor the effect of tobacco on respiration. The amounts of oxygen, O2​, and carbon monoxide, CO, were measured in blood leaving the lungs of smokers and nonsmokers, and the results are shown in the table below.What can you conclude concerning the effect of tobacco on the formation of oxyhemoglobin HbO2​ and HbCO?\nI. Tobacco has no effect on the formation of HbO2​ and HbCO.\nII. Tobacco increases the formation of HbO2​.\nIII. Tobacco decreases the formation of HbO2​.\nIV. Tobacco increases the formation of HbCO.\nV. Tobacco decreases the formation of HbCO.", "options": ["I only", "II and IV", "II and V", "III and IV", "III and V"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": "Yes (Table)"}, {"id": "est-old-1-q62", "text": "Individuals with multiple sclerosis have their immune system attack the myelin sheath of the neurons found in the central nervous system. How would damage to the myelin sheath affect the transmission of nervous messages?", "options": ["Nervous messages would be transmitted normally since the neurons are not destroyed.", "Nervous messages would be transmitted faster since the presence of myelin sheath decreases the speed of the nervous message.", "Nervous messages would be transmitted slower since the presence of myelin sheath increases the speed of the nervous message.", "The transmission of nervous messages would start at a fast speed and then decrease.", "The transmission of nervous messages would start at a slow speed and then increase."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q65", "text": "The amount of mitochondria as a percentage of total cell volume is measured in the atria and ventricles of the heart. The amount of mitochondria present in the cells of the left ventricle is 49%, while that in the cells of the left atrium is 35%. How can you explain the difference in the amount of mitochondria in atria and ventricles?\nI. The size of atrium is smaller than the size of ventricles.\nII. The atrium pumps blood a very short distance, while the ventricle pumps blood a long distance.\nIII. The atrium needs less force to pump blood than the ventricle.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "I and II", "II and III", "I, II and III"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q68", "text": "The primary role of yellow bone marrow and the reason it is yellow is", "options": ["to produce white blood cells.", "to produce red blood cells.", "to produce plasma.", "to store calcium.", "to store fats."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q76", "text": "Certain individuals present a goiter, which is an abnormal increase in the volume of the neck due to malfunction of the thyroid gland. Several studies were done in order to study the effect of consuming iodine rich meals on the function of the thyroid gland and the appearance of goiter. The document below shows the percentage of goiter with respect to the concentration of iodine in two different populations.Based on the results of the above document, what can you conclude concerning the effect of iodine on the appearance of goiter?", "options": ["High amounts of iodine in the meal causes malfunction of the thyroid gland, which leads to the appearance of goiter.", "Low amounts of iodine in the meal causes malfunction of the thyroid gland, which leads to the appearance of goiter.", "Low amounts of iodine in the meal improves the function of the thyroid gland, and goiter won't appear.", "High amounts of iodine in the meal improves the function of the thyroid gland, which leads to the appearance of goiter.", "The amount of iodine in the meal has no effect on the thyroid gland and goiter."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": "Yes (Table)"}, {"id": "est-old-2-q16", "text": "Which of the following is NOT true about blood circulation?", "options": ["Deoxygenated blood is pumped by the right ventricle to the lungs through the pulmonary artery.", "Oxygenated blood reaches the left atrium by the pulmonary vein.", "All arteries carry oxygenated blood except the pulmonary artery.", "All veins carry deoxygenated blood except the pulmonary vein.", "The right part of the heart has oxygenated blood, while the left part has deoxygenated blood."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q42", "text": "Raises blood calcium", "options": ["Glucagon hormone", "Antidiuretic hormone", "Parathyroid hormone", "Thyroid hormone", "Insulin hormone"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q43", "text": "Promotes water retention", "options": ["Glucagon hormone", "Antidiuretic hormone", "Parathyroid hormone", "Thyroid hormone", "Insulin hormone"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q44", "text": "Lowers blood glucose", "options": ["Glucagon hormone", "Antidiuretic hormone", "Parathyroid hormone", "Thyroid hormone", "Insulin hormone"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q52", "text": "The following bar graph shows the amount of food X in different organs of the digestive system.We can conclude that the type of food X is", "options": ["sucrose.", "starch.", "lipids.", "protein.", "maltose."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 300\" width=\"100%\" height=\"300\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\">\n    <text x=\"63\" y=\"65\">10</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"145\">5</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"233\">0</text>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#2563eb\">\n    <rect x=\"95\"  y=\"60\"  width=\"28\" height=\"170\"/>\n    <rect x=\"175\" y=\"60\"  width=\"28\" height=\"170\"/>\n    <rect x=\"255\" y=\"125\" width=\"28\" height=\"105\"/>\n    <rect x=\"335\" y=\"212\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"109\" y=\"255\">Ingestion</text>\n    <line x1=\"109\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"109\" y2=\"235\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n    <text x=\"189\" y=\"250\">Mouth</text>\n    <text x=\"269\" y=\"250\">Stomach</text>\n    <text x=\"349\" y=\"250\">Small Intestine</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"-135\" y=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\">Amount of food X (g)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-2-q67", "text": "The amount of mitochondria in the left ventricle is more than the that in the left atrium. How can you explain this variation in the amount of mitochondria?\nI. The size of the ventricle is bigger than the size of the atrium.\nII. The left ventricle pumps the blood with larger force to all parts; therefore, it needs a larger amount of energy produced by cellular respiration.\nIII. The left atrium pumps blood to the left ventricle with less force than that of the left ventricle; therefore, it needs less amount of energy produced by cellular respiration.\nIV. The left atrium pumps the blood with more force to all body parts; therefore, it needs a big amount of energy produced by cellular respiration.", "options": ["I only", "I and II", "I and IV", "II and III", "I, II and III"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 300\" width=\"100%\" height=\"300\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"end\">\n    <text x=\"53\" y=\"55\">50</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"90\">40</text>\n    <text x=\"53\" y=\"125\">30</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"160\">20</text>\n    <text x=\"53\" y=\"195\">10</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"233\">0</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"0.8\">\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"50\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"85\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"120\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"155\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"155\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"190\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#1d4ed8\">\n    <rect x=\"90\"  y=\"58\"  width=\"36\" height=\"172\"/>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"97\"  width=\"36\" height=\"133\"/>\n    <rect x=\"250\" y=\"163\" width=\"36\" height=\"67\"/>\n    <rect x=\"330\" y=\"195\" width=\"36\" height=\"35\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"108\" y=\"246\">Heart,</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"258\">Left ventricle</text>\n    <text x=\"188\" y=\"246\">Heart,</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"258\">Left atrium</text>\n    <text x=\"268\" y=\"248\">Liver</text>\n    <text x=\"348\" y=\"248\">Pituitary gland</text>\n    <text x=\"240\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Organs</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"-135\" y=\"25\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\">Mitochondrial distribution %</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-2-q70", "text": "The following document shows different experiments done in vitro to study the digestion of lipids.According to the data in the above graphic, bile", "options": ["digests lipids into fatty acids and glycerol.", "emulsifies lipids to make it easier for the enzymes to digest lipids.", "digests and emulsifies lipids.", "maintains the temperature of the tube.", "has no effect on the digestion of lipids."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 260\" width=\"100%\" height=\"260\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(40, 20)\">\n    <rect x=\"25\" y=\"30\" width=\"40\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 26 80 L 26 130 A 9 9 0 0 0 64 130 L 64 80 Z\" fill=\"#93c5fd\" opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n    <rect x=\"26\" y=\"55\" width=\"38\" height=\"25\" fill=\"#fde047\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n    <text x=\"45\" y=\"160\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n    <text x=\"45\" y=\"175\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Water + Oil</text>\n    <text x=\"45\" y=\"195\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#64748b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oil layer</text>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(190, 20)\">\n    <rect x=\"25\" y=\"30\" width=\"40\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <p