oyed</text>\n    <text x=\"410\" y=\"93\">Insufficient amount</text>\n    <text x=\"597\" y=\"93\">Normal</text>\n\n    <text x=\"82\" y=\"137\" font-weight=\"bold\">Individual B</text>\n    <text x=\"230\" y=\"137\">Normal</text>\n    <text x=\"410\" y=\"137\">Normal amount</text>\n    <text x=\"597\" y=\"130\">Most of receptors are</text>\n    <text x=\"597\" y=\"145\">destroyed</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-3-q44", "text": "Which statement is true about bile?\nI. Bile is secreted by the liver and stored in the gallbladder.\nII. Bile is secreted by the small intestine and stored in the gallbladder.\nIII. Bile emulsifies lipids.\nIV. Bile neutralizes the digested food coming from the stomach to small intestine.", "options": ["I and III", "I and IV", "II and III", "I, III, and IV", "II, III, and IV"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-3-q52", "text": "The body of an athlete depends on food to obtain the energy needed for its cellular activity and to build new matter. In order to determine which food best supplies the body with the required energy, an experiment was performed to measure muscular exhaustion.  Which conclusion can be drawn from the above experiment?", "options": ["An athlete should have meals rich in lipids and proteins for the best performance.", "An athlete should have meals rich in carbohydrates for the best performance.", "An athlete should never have a carbohydrate meal before performance.", "An athlete should have a balanced diet for the best performance.", "There is no relation between the kinds of ingested foods and the performance of an athlete."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 200\" width=\"100%\" height=\"200\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"490\" heigh