me changes in temperature and pH."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q54", "text": "Which of the following statements correctly identifies the charge of a subatomic particle and best describes the location of that particle in the atom?", "options": ["An electron is positive, and it is located outside the nucleus.", "An electron is negative, and it is located inside the nucleus.", "A proton has no charge, and it is located outside the nucleus.", "A neutron has no charge, and it is located inside the nucleus."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q56", "text": "When cells hydrolyze ATP, releasing energy, which of the following bonds in the ATP molecule is typically broken?", "options": ["The bond between 2 phosphate groups", "The bond between ribose and a phosphate group", "The bond between adenine and ribose", "The bond between adenine and a phosphate group"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q65", "text": "Which of these types of molecules is composed of a 5-carbon sugar (pentose), phosphate group, and nitrogenous base?", "options": ["Amino acid", "Fatty acid", "Monosaccharide", "Nucleotide"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q68", "text": "Molecule X and Molecule Y have slightly different shapes. An enzyme reacts with Molecule X, but it does not react with Molecule Y. Based on this information, which of the following statements best explains this difference in the reactivity of the enzyme with these 2 molecules?", "options": ["Molecule X has less energy, making it more attractive for the enzyme.", "Molecule X transfers protons that allow the enzyme to work.", "Molecule Y does not require the enzyme to break down.", "Molecule Y does not fit properly into the active site."], "answe