\" y=\"298\">10</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"298\">20</text>\n    <text x=\"315\" y=\"298\">30</text><text x=\"390\" y=\"298\">40</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"240\" y=\"325\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Concentration of Sucrose (mmol/L)</text>\n  <text x=\"-160\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\">Rate of Sucrose Uptake (μmol/g/min)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-1-q34", "text": "The process by which water diffuses through a selectively permeable membrane is known as", "options": ["diffusion.", "osmosis.", "active transport.", "transpiration.", "evaporation."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q43", "text": "A cucumber is placed in a jar containing a salt solution. After few days, the cucumber shrinks. What is the probable reason behind the shrinkage of the cucumber?", "options": ["The cucumber is placed in a hypertonic solution, so water diffuses outside the cucumber cells.", "The cucumber is placed in a hypotonic solution, so water diffuses outside the cucumber cells.", "The cucumber is placed in a hypertonic solution, so water diffuses inside the cucumber cells.", "The cucumber is placed in a hypotonic solution, so water diffuses inside the cucumber cells.", "The cucumber is placed in an isotonic solution, so water diffuses outside the cucumber cells."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q1", "text": "The site of cellular respiration in the eukaryotic cells is called", "options": ["smooth endoplasmic reticulum.", "golgi bodies.", "mitochondria.", "ribosomes.", "chloroplasts."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q10", "text": "When a red blood cell is placed in a hypo