, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q9", "text": "Based on the figure below, the following conclusion can be made:", "options": ["Glucose is a hydrophobic molecule and thus cannot pass through the phospholipid bilayer.", "The passage of glucose requires ATP.", "The passage of glucose mostly occurs against the concentration gradient.", "The cell is placed in a hypotonic solution.", "Glucose can enter the cell through facilitated diffusion."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"35\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">cell exterior</text>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"195\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">cell interior</text>\n  <g fill=\"#94a3b8\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"1\">\n    <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"74\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"410\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"422\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"434\" cy=\"80\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"140\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"140\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"74\" cy=\"140\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"410\" cy=\"140\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"422\" cy=\"140\" r=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"434\" cy=\"140\" r=\"5\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(110, 65)\">\n    <path d=\"M 15 15 C 5 25, 5 65, 15 75 C 25 75, 25 25, 35 15 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 55 15 C 65 25, 65 65, 55 75 C 45 75, 45 25, 35 15 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"35,15 42,27 35,35 28,27\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(210, 65)\">\n    <path d=\"M 15 15 C 5 35, 5 55, 15 75 C 30 65, 30 25, 15 15 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 55 15 C 65 35, 65 55, 55 75 C 40 65, 40 25, 55 15 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"35,40 42,48 35,56 28,48\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(310, 65)\">\n    <path d=\"M 15 15 C 25 25, 25 65, 15 75 C 5 65, 5 25, 15 15 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 55 15 C 45 25, 45 65, 55 75 C 65 65, 65 25, 55 15 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"35,65 42,73 35,81 28,73\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"145\" y=\"45\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f59e0b\">glucose</text>\n  <line x1=\"145\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"145\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-4-q29", "text": "Which of the following is a logical hypothesis BASED on the graph shown?", "options": ["Mitochondria are found the most in muscle cells.", "White blood cells have more mitochondria than red blood cells.", "Cardiac cells have mitochondria that are larger in size compared to skin cells.", "The number of mitochondria will increase as we exercise.", "Bone cells do not need to have any mitochondria."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 300\" width=\"100%\" height=\"300\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9.5\" text-anchor=\"end\">\n    <text x=\"63\" y=\"45\">5</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"93\">2.5</text>\n    <text x=\"63\" y=\"140\">1.25</text><text x=\"63\" y=\"233\">0</text>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#2563eb\">\n    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"137\" width=\"36\" height=\"93\"/>\n    <rect x=\"180\" y=\"42\"  width=\"36\" height=\"188\"/>\n    <rect x=\"340\" y=\"222\" width=\"36\" height=\"8\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\n    <text x=\"118\" y=\"250\">Liver</text>\n    <text x=\"198\" y=\"250\">Cardiac</text>\n    <text x=\"278\" y=\"250\">Red Blood</text>\n    <text x=\"358\" y=\"250\">Skin</text>\n    <text x=\"238\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Types of Cells</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"-135\" y=\"22\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\">Number of Mitochondria ×10³</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-4-q47", "text": "All of the following molecules can pass through the plasma membrane by simple diffusion EXCEPT", "options": ["oxygen", "carbondioxide", "glucose", "A and B", "A and C"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q64", "text": "Which of these structures is found in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes?", "options": ["Rough endoplasmic reticulum", "Nucleus", "Cellulose", "Ribosomes", "Chloroplast"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q73", "text": "Which organelle(s) is/are surrounded by a double membrane?\nI. Nucleus\nII. Golgi body\nIII. Ribosome\nIV. Mitochondria", "options": ["I only", "II only", "IV only", "I and IV only", "I, III, and IV only"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q8", "text": "Red blood cells are placed in three solutions of different concentrations. The microscopic observations of these cells are done, and the results are shown in the following table.Consider that the cytoplasm of red blood cells has a concentration of 9 grams/100cc. Which statement is INCORRECT?", "options": ["The red blood cells lyse in solution 1 because the water passes by osmosis from the exterior hypotonic medium into the interior hypertonic medium.", "The red blood cells lyse because the cytoplasmic concentration is less than that of solution 1, thus leading to enormous turgidity.", "The red blood cells remain normal in solution 2 because both the intracellular and extracellular media are isotonic.", "The red blood cells shrink because water exits from the hypotonic medium to the hypertonic medium by plasmolysis in solution 3.", "The red blood cells don't lyse because there is no exchange that occurs between the two media in solution 2."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"630\" height=\"135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"220\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"365\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"510\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0f172a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"122\" y=\"47\">Solution number</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"47\">1</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"47\">2</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"47\">3</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#0f172a\">\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"85\" font-weight=\"bold\">Concentration of the</text>\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"99\" font-weight=\"bold\">solution in % (g/cc)</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.03</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.09</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\">26</text>\n\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"130\" font-weight=\"bold\">Aspect of red blood</text>\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"145\" font-weight=\"bold\">cells</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red blood cells</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bulge and lyse</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red blood cells</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\">remain normal</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red blood cells</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\">shrink</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-5-q69", "text": "A kind of microorganism X is cultured in a test tube on a chemical medium composed of water and mineral ions. When this tube is placed in the light and in the dark, X does not multiply. When sucrose is added to the liquid, X multiplies.  Microorganism X is", "options": ["photoautotroph.", "heterotroph.", "composed of chlorophyll.", "mixotrophic.", "photoautotroph or chemoautotroph."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-1-q49", "text": "A researcher isolates a cell and observes that it contains a large number of lysosomes. What type of cell is most likely being observed?", "options": ["Neuron", "Muscle cell", "Phagocytic white blood cell", "Red blood cell", "Epithelial cell"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-2-q29", "text": "Which of these structures is found in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes?", "options": ["Plasmid", "Nucleus", "Mitochondria", "Ribosomes", "Chloroplast"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-2-q45", "text": "Which of the following terms best describes the movement of molecules from a medium of low concentration to a medium of high concentration with the use of energy?", "options": ["Diffusion", "Osmosis", "Active transport", "Facilitated diffusion", "Exocytosis"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-2-q47", "text": "The synthesis of ribosomes occurs in the", "options": ["rough endoplasmic reticulum", "smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "nucleus", "nucleolus", "golgi bodies"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-2-q57", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be drawn about the size of living cells?", "options": ["The size of prokaryotic cells is larger than the size of eukaryotic cells, with the Bacillus bacteria having the largest size.", "The size of prokaryotic cells is larger than the size of eukaryotic cells, with the Streptococcus pneumonia bacteria having the largest size.", "The size of eukaryotic cells is larger than the size of prokaryotic cells, but only the Bacillus bacteria have a size approximately equal to that of eukaryotic cells.", "The size of eukaryotic cells is larger than the size of prokaryotic cells, but only the Streptococcus pneumonia bacteria have a size approximately equal to that of eukaryotic cells.", "The size of eukaryotic cells is larger than the size of prokaryotic cells."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 240\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:500px;height:auto;background:#F4F1E6;border-radius:4px;\">\n  <style>\n    .axis{stroke:#16232A;stroke-width:2px;}\n    .tick{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;fill:#16232A;text-anchor:middle;}\n    .axlbl{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;fill:#16232A;text-anchor:middle;}\n    .prok{fill:#C98A2C;}\n    .euk{fill:#3F7D5C;}\n    .name{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;fill:#16232A;text-anchor:start;}\n    .grouplbl{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;fill:#16232A;}\n  </style>\n\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"20\" class=\"grouplbl\">Prokaryotic cells (0.5–4 µm)</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"30\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" class=\"prok\"/>\n  <text x=\"145\" y=\"43\" class=\"name\">S. pneumoniae — 0.5 to 1.25 µm</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"55\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" class=\"prok\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"68\" class=\"name\">Bacillus — 1 to 4 µm</text>\n\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"105\" class=\"grouplbl\">Eukaryotic cells (10–100 µm)</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"115\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" class=\"euk\"/>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"128\" class=\"name\">Animal cell — 10 to 30 µm</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"140\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" class=\"euk\"/>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"153\" class=\"name\">Sperm cell — 50 to 65 µm</text>\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"165\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" class=\"euk\"/>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"178\" class=\"name\">Plant cell — 10 to 100 µm</text>\n\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"220\" class=\"axlbl\" style=\"text-anchor:start;font-weight:600;\">Eukaryotic cells are roughly 10× to 100× larger than prokaryotic cells</text>\n</svg>"}, {"id": "est-new-3-q16", "text": "What will happen after a few minutes if an animal cell having an intracellular concentration of 0.3 mol/L is submerged in a solution with a concentration of 0.8 mol/L?", "options": ["Osmosis: Water will diffuse from the intracellular medium to the extracellular medium.", "Osmosis: Water will diffuse from the extracellular medium to the intracellular medium.", "Diffusion: Solute particles will diffuse from the intracellular medium to the extracellular medium.", "Diffusion: Solute particles will diffuse from the extracellular medium to the intracellular medium.", "Neither water nor the solute will diffuse."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q27", "text": "Which organelle is responsible for packaging and modifying proteins for secretion?", "options": ["Nucleus", "Golgi apparatus", "Lysosome", "Endoplasmic reticulum", "Mitochondrion"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q28", "text": "Which of the following correctly describes the presence and composition of a cell wall?", "options": ["Found in animal cells and composed of chitin", "Found in animal cells and composed of cellulose", "Found in plant cells and composed of chitin", "Found in plant cells ad composed of cellulose", "Found in both animal and plant cells and composed of cellulose"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q45", "text": "What is the role of mitochondria?", "options": ["They synthesize lipids.", "They synthesize ribosomes.", "They are the site where cellular respiration occurs.", "They are the site where photosynthesis occurs.", "They are the site where synthesized proteins are modified."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q55", "text": "(Table) What can you conclude from the above information? (Number of mitochondria in cells)", "options": ["Skin cells produce the biggest amount of energy.", "Liver cells produce the biggest amount of energy.", "Muscle cells produce more energy than liver cells.", "Muscle cells produce the biggest amount of energy.", "Liver cells produce the least amount of energy."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    subgraph Energy [\"Mitochondria Content (Energy Production)\"]\n        L_mito[\"Liver (1000) > Muscle (765) > Skin (200)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Protein [\"Ribosome Content (Protein Synthesis)\"]\n        P_ribo[\"Pancreas (3.0M) > Liver (2.5M) > Kidney (1.5M)\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q6", "text": "What structure is responsible for producing ATP through cellular respiration?", "options": ["Ribosome", "Nucleus", "Mitochondrion", "Plasma membrane"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q7", "text": "What structure regulates the movement of substances into and out of the cell?", "options": ["Ribosome", "Nucleus", "Mitochondrion", "Plasma membrane"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q8", "text": "What structure contains the cell's genetic material?", "options": ["Ribosome", "Nucleus", "Mitochondrion", "Plasma membrane"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q9", "text": "What structure is the site of translation where proteins are assembled from mRNA?", "options": ["Ribosome", "Nucleus", "Mitochondrion", "Plasma membrane"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q10", "text": "What structure is the location of DNA replication and transcription?", "options": ["Ribosome", "Nucleus", "Mitochondrion", "Plasma membrane"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q16", "text": "A living cell is placed in a beaker containing a solution with a concentration of 5 mmol/L... What do you think might happen after a few hours?", "options": ["Osmosis of water from intracellular to extracellular medium will occur, and the cell will shrink.", "Osmosis of water from intracellular to extracellular medium will occur, and the cell will swell.", "Osmosis of water from extracellular to intracellular medium will occur, and the cell will shrink.", "Osmosis of water from extracellular to intracellular medium will occur, and the cell will swell.", "Diffusion of solute particles from extracellular to intracellular medium, and the cell will swell."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q9", "text": "Which structure is not correctly paired with its function?", "options": ["Ribosome - protein synthesis", "Mitochondria - energy production.", "Golgi body - protein packing.", "Centrioles - genetic information."], "answer": 3, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q19", "text": "Plants and cyanobacteria are photosynthetic organisms, how do the student know if that organism is plant or cyanobacteria?", "options": ["Plant cells have nucleus, cyanobacteria do not have nucleus.", "Plant cells have chlorophyll, but cyanobacteria do not have.", "Cyanobacteria have cell wall, but plant do not have.", "Cyanobacteria have ribosome, but plant do not have."], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q22", "text": "Some molecules travel through cell membrane against concentration gradient, this type of transport called:", "options": ["Passive transport.", "Osmosis.", "Active transport.", "Pinocytosis."], "answer": 2, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q24", "text": "Why does the Animal cell that placed in distilled water lysis?", "options": ["Water flow into the cell.", "Water flow out of the cell.", "Solute flow out of the cell.", "Solute flow into the cell."], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q34", "text": "Short microtubule that is found in paramecium in great number:", "options": ["Flagella", "Cilia", "Sarcomere", "Actin"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q41", "text": "Which of the following statements about cell structure is NOT correct?", "options": ["Plant cells have cell walls, whereas animal cells do not.", "Ribosome are the main sites of energy production for the cell.", "Plant cells have chloroplasts, whereas animal cells do not.", "Lysosomes function in the digestion of cellular waste products."], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q44", "text": "What would happen to a human red blood cell if placed in distilled water?", "options": ["It would shrivel.", "It would plasmolysis.", "It would lyse.", "It would not be affected."], "answer": 2, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q59", "text": "Damage to the Golgi apparatus will most likely have which of the following cellular effects?", "options": ["Transcription will be limited to cytoplasmic vesicles of the damaged cells", "Translation will be limited within cytoplasmic vesicles of the damaged cells", "Protein products will be modified for use inside the damaged cells.", "Protein products will not be secreted from the damaged cells."], "answer": 3, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q68", "text": "What's the role of flagella?", "options": ["Propulsion", "Cell division", "Protein synthesis", "Photosynthesis"], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q79", "text": "Apoptosis is one of the functions of", "options": ["Ribosomes", "Centrosomes", "Lysosome", "Mitochondria"], "answer": 2, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q81", "text": "What is common in mitochondria and endoplasmic reticulum membrane?", "options": ["ATP", "Lipids", "Proteins", "Starch"], "answer": 2, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q97", "text": "What is the difference between cilia and flagella?", "options": ["Cilia is shorter and greater in number", "Cilia is longer and less in number", "Both have same length and number", "No difference in number and length between them"], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q6", "text": "Which of the following is a major difference between prokaryotic cell and eukaryotic cell?", "options": ["only prokaryotes have nuclei.", "only prokaryotic have photosynthetic pigments.", "only eukaryotic have method of locomotion", "only eukaryotic have membrane bound organelles."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q15", "text": "by which process do cells use energy to move substance across a membrane against concentration gradient", "options": ["active transport", "diffusion", "osmosis", "passive transport"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q25", "text": "In this figure, a dialysis bag containing a 30% starch solution is placed into a beaker of distilled water. The dialysis bag is permeable to water but is not permeable to starch. Which of the following statement concerning the initial movement of water molecules is correct?", "options": ["More water molecules will move from the beaker of distilled water into the bag than in opposite side.", "More water molecules move from bag to beaker of distilled water than in the opposite side.", "Water molecules will not move through the dialysis membrane.", "Equal numbers of water molecules will move in both directions."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmln