": null}, {"id": "act-2-q34", "text": "What is the correct order of protein production? 1) Ribosome. 2) Endoplasmic reticulum. 3) Secretory vesicles. 4) Golgi apparatus.", "options": ["1,2,3,4", "2,4,3,1", "1,2,4,3", "3,2,4,1"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q36", "text": "What is a different between animal and plant cell?", "options": ["Plant cell has centrioles, animal cell has not.", "Plant cell has cell wall, animal cell does not.", "Animal cell has mitochondria, plant cell does not.", "Animal cell has cell membrane, plant cell does not."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q100", "text": "A protein synthesized in the ribosome then moved to ER then to transport vesicles then to Golgi apparatus then to secretory vesicles. Which structure will the protein transported to?", "options": ["Mitochondria.", "Chloroplast.", "Nucleus.", "Cell membrane"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q3", "text": "if the cell lost its ability to pump the solute out of the cell membrane, solute concentration inside will be greater than outside. What will be the effect on the transfer of water?", "options": ["move in by osmosis.", "move in by active transport", "move out by osmosis", "move out by active transport."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q4", "text": "protein made to be exported. Which organelle will it go to first?", "options": ["Endoplasmic reticulum (Rough ER) / Ribosome", "Lysosome", "Vacuole", "Golgi apparatus."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q10", "text": "scientist take cells from patient to know type of infection, he observed 3 types of cells. Patient cells, fungi cells, and bacterial cells. Types of cel