h pole<br>6 chromatids pulled to South pole\"]\n    A --> D[\"Daughter Cells (6 chromosomes each)\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q35", "text": "A diploid tomato plant cell has 24 chromosomes. How many chromosomes will each daughter cell have at the end of mitosis?", "options": ["24 chromosomes of 2 chromatids", "24 chromosomes of 1 chromatid", "12 chromosomes of 2 chromatids", "12 chromosomes of 1 chromatid", "48 chromosomes of 1 chromatid"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q38", "text": "During an experiment, a student observes a cell where all chromosomes are lined up at the center of the cell. Based on this information, which stage of cell cycle is the cell most likely in?", "options": ["Prophase", "Anaphase", "Interphase", "Metaphase", "Telophase"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q21", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be drawn concerning the length of the life cycle of the plant cell?", "options": ["The cell cycle is fastest when the environmental temperature is 10°C.", "The cell cycle is fastest when the environmental temperature ranges between 10°C and 12°C.", "The cell cycle becomes slower as the temperature increases.", "The cell cycle becomes faster as the temperature increases.", "Environmental temperature has no effect on the duration of the cell cycle."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    T1[\"10°C: 70.2 hours (Slow)\"] --> T2[\"14°C: 62.0 hours\"]\n    T2 --> T3[\"18°C: 50.2 hours (Fastest)\"]\n    T1 & T2 & T3 --> Trend[\"Conclusion: Duration decreases / Cell cycle accelerates as temperature rises\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q27", "text": "Which of the following is true about crossing over?", "options": ["Crossing over occurs between sister chromatids.", "Crossing over leads to increased genetic diversity.", "Crossing over reduces genetic variation.", "Crossing over only occurs in meiosis II.", "Crossing over results in identical daughter cells."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q32", "text": "How many divisions should a cell undergo to obtain 16 cells?", "options": ["4 divisions", "6 divisions", "8 divisions", "12 divisions", "32 divisions"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q34", "text": "If the amount of DNA in a cell obtained at the end of mitosis is 3.3 a.u., then", "options": ["the amount of DNA in this cell is 6.6 a.u. during G₁ of Interphase and 3.3 a.u. during G₂.", "the amount of DNA in this cell is 6.6 a.u. during G₁ and during S phase of interphase.", "the amount of DNA in this cell is 3.3 a.u. during G₁ and end of S phase of interphase.", "the amount of DNA in this cell is 3.3 a.u. during G₂ and during S phase of interphase.", "the amount of DNA in this cell is 6.6 a.u. during G₂ of Interphase and 3.3 a.u. during G₁."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q51", "text": "(Meiosis Diagram) Which phase of meiosis is shown in the above figure?", "options": ["Metaphase I", "Telophase I", "Anaphase I", "Anaphase II", "Metaphase II"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph TD\n    Parent[\"Parent Cell (2n = 6 duplicated chromosomes)\"]\n    Parent --> Ana1[\"Anaphase I (Separation of homologous pairs)\"]\n    Ana1 --> Inter[\"Telophase I / Meiosis II\"]\n    Inter --> Gametes[\"4 Haploid Gametes (n = 3 single chromosomes each)\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q52", "text": "(Meiosis Diagram) How many chromosomes will be obtained in each daughter cell at the end of meiosis done by the cell shown above?", "options": ["3 chromosomes", "6 chromosomes", "