 ACT - CAA"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q5", "text": "All of the following statements are true about RNA processing EXCEPT:", "options": ["It takes place in the cytoplasm.", "As a result, the mRNA becomes shorter.", "Introns are cut out during the process.", "It takes place after transcription.", "Exons are spliced together to form the final mRNA."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q37", "text": "DNA in a cell has 24% of guanine. Based on Chargaff's Rule, what is the percentage of adenine found in this DNA?", "options": ["24%", "26%", "48%", "52%", "76%"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q46", "text": "The following is a normal DNA sequence followed by a mutant DNA sequence.Normal DNA: A T T C C G T A CMutant DNA: A T T C G G T A CThis type of mutation is:", "options": ["deletion", "inversion", "insertion", "substitution", "translocation"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q59", "text": "During transcription, which RNA bases would pair with the following transcribed DNA sequence A G C C T?", "options": ["T C G C A", "U C G G A", "T G G G T", "U G C C A", "T C G G U"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q65", "text": "Which enzyme is responsible for unwinding the DNA double helix during replication?", "options": ["Helicase", "DNA polymerase", "RNA polymerase", "Ligase", "Primase"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q10", "text": "A biology class was performing an experiment in the lab. The students had obtained a DNA strand with radioactive thymine. Later, as they left the strand in a medium for multiplication, they realized that the radioactivity was observed only in part of the DNA and not all DNA molecules.  The process was explained by the teacher as", "options": ["DNA translation.", "cell proliferation.", "semi-conservative replication of DNA.", "conservative replication of DNA.", "semi-conservative translation of DNA."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q17", "text": "A DNA nucleotide consists of", "options": ["phosphate group, deoxyribose sugar, and nitrogenous base (A, C, G or U).", "phosphate group, ribose sugar, and nitrogenous base (A, C, G or T).", "phosphate group, deoxyribose sugar, and nitrogenous base (A, T, G or U).", "phosphate group, deoxyribose sugar, and nitrogenous base (A, C, G or T).", "phosphate group, deoxyribose sugar, and nitrogenous base (T, C, G or U)."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q28", "text": "The best definition of a gene is:", "options": ["a sequence of amino acids which makes up a polypeptide", "a sequence of ribonucleotides which makes up a DNA and codes for polypeptide", "a sequence of deoxyribonucleotides which makes up the DNA and is transcribed to RNA then translated to a polypeptide", "any sequence of deoxyribonucleotides which makes up the DNA", "any sequence of ribonucleotides which makes up a DNA"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q36", "text": "A DNA molecule has 20% A and 30% G. The total number of nucleotides in the DNA molecule is 20. The number of thymine nitrogenous bases in the DNA is", "options": ["2", "3", "4", "5", "6"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q44", "text": "Which of the following statements best explains the fact that a mutation in a cell's DNA does not always result in an error in the polypeptide produced from that DNA sequence?", "options": ["Some polypeptides are produced by a code other than a nucleic acid code.", "The nucleolus can repair damaged DNA.", "The Golgi body can repair damaged DNA.", "Each amino acid is coded by more than one codon.", "Scientists have no idea why this phenomenon occurs."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q54", "text": "The document below represents the normal and the mutant DNA sequence coding for a protein.Normal DNA sequence: TAT CAT CCT AAG GTAMutant DNA sequence: TAT CAT CGT AAG GTAThe mutation that affects the DNA sequence is known as", "options": ["mutation by substitution.", "mutation by deletion.", "mutation by addition.", "silent mutation due to a deletion mutation.", "mutation by insertion."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-1-q1", "text": "What process uses mRNA as a template to produce amino acid chains?", "options": ["Photosynthesis", "Cellular respiration", "Mitosis", "Protein synthesis"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-1-q54", "text": "(Graph) Ribosomes are structures found in living cells... What conclusion can be derived from the above graph?", "options": ["The cell that has more ribosomes produces less protein.", "The cell that has more ribosomes produces more protein.", "The cell produces the same amount of protein, no matter what the number of ribosomes is.", "As the number of ribosomes doubles, the process of protein synthesis decreases by half.", "As protein synthesis increases, the number of ribosomes in the cell increases."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 240\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-wid