 pos 10| S3[\"Sequence 3:<br>5'-ATG CCG TTA AGA CTG A-3'<br>(Frameshift & count change)\"]\n    WT -->|Base deletion -T at pos 13| S4[\"Sequence 4:<br>5'-ATG CCG TTA GAC GA-3'<br>(Frameshift & count change)\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q56", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be derived from the results presented in the above table? (Number of ribosomes in body cells)", "options": ["Pancreatic cells undergo protein synthesis more than liver cells, which in turn undergo more protein synthesis than kidney cells.", "Kidney cells undergo protein synthesis more than liver cells, which in turn undergo more protein synthesis than pancreatic cells.", "Kidney cells undergo protein synthesis more than pancreatic cells, which in turn undergo more protein synthesis than liver cells.", "Pancreatic cells undergo protein synthesis more than kidney cells, which in turn undergo more protein synthesis than liver cells.", "Liver cells undergo protein synthesis more than kidney cells, which in turn undergo more protein synthesis than pancreatic cells."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    subgraph Energy [\"Mitochondria Content (Energy Production)\"]\n        L_mito[\"Liver (1000) > Muscle (765) > Skin (200)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Protein [\"Ribosome Content (Protein Synthesis)\"]\n        P_ribo[\"Pancreas (3.0M) > Liver (2.5M) > Kidney (1.5M)\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q55", "text": "Which of the following sequences could never be part of mRNA?", "options": ["AUCCGA", "CCGATA", "GCAUAA", "GCAGAC", "ACGUCG"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q2", "text": "Every DNA molecule replicate as one old strand and one new strand, so DNA replication is described as:", "options": ["Conservative.", "Semi-conservative.", "Transcribed.", "Translated."], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "