": ["Protein exported outside the cell", "Nucleic acid exported outside the cell", "Protein transported to mitochondria", "Nucleic acid transported to mitochondria"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q69", "text": "Scientists used many observations to determine the structure of the DNA molecule. Which of the following observations provided the strong evidence that guanine form hydrogen bonds with cytosine, as opposed to forming hydrogen bonds with adenine or thymine?", "options": ["The same carbon-based ring structure is present in both guanine and cytosine", "The percentage of guanine bases equals the percentage of cytosine", "The same type of sugar molecule attaches to guanine as attaches to cytosine", "The number of deoxyribose molecules equals the number of guanine and cytosine bases combined"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q6", "text": "In 1956, Arthur Kornberg isolated DNA polymerase, an enzyme that replicates DNA. In which of the following eukaryotic cellular components is DNA polymerase typically active?", "options": ["Centriole", "Nucleus", "Lysosome", "Ribosome"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q12", "text": "In 1958, Meselson and Stahl determined that the process of DNA replication is semi-conservative. In DNA molecules produced by semi-conservative DNA replication, each double helix contains:", "options": ["2 new strands of DNA", "2 parental strands of DNA", "1 new strand of DNA and 1 new strand of RNA", "1 new strand of DNA and 1 parental strand of DNA"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q21", "text": "Specialized cells of the pancreas produce insulin. Which of the following observations most strongly supports the conclusion that it 