ses as the intensity of light increases.\nIII. In sun plants, the rate of photosynthesis increases as the intensity of light increases.\nIV. In shade plants, the rate of photosynthesis is not affected by light.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "III only", "I and III", "III and IV"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 350\" width=\"100%\" height=\"350\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <defs>\n    <pattern id=\"grid8\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\">\n      <path d=\"M 25 0 L 0 0 0 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#dcdcdc\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n    </pattern>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"40\" width=\"375\" height=\"220\" fill=\"url(#grid8)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"470,256 480,260 470,264\" fill=\"#000000\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"76,30 80,20 84,30\" fill=\"#000000\"/>\n  <text x=\"260\" y=\"295\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Light Intensity</text>\n  <text x=\"-150\" y=\"35\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\">Rate Of Photosynthesis</text>\n  <path d=\"M 80 260 C 100 190, 140 150, 220 145 C 300 145, 380 145, 450 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2b5c8f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"390\" y=\"138\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2b5c8f\" font-weight=\"bold\">Shade plants</text>\n  <path d=\"M 80 260 C 130 210, 200 140, 310 100 C 370 85, 420 80, 450 78\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"390\" y=\"70\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#c0392b\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sun plants</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-1-q23", "text": "________ is a process by which plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to create oxygen and energy in the form of sugar.", "options": ["Fermentation", "Glycolysis", "Chemosynthesis", "Photosynthesis", "Krebs cycle"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q25", "text": "A plant is placed in the light, supplied with water, and covered with a transparent air tight jar. What might happen to the rate of photosynthesis if this plant is kept at this condition for several days?", "options": ["The rate of photosynthesis increases since the plant is exposed to light for a long period of time.", "The rate of photosynthesis decreases since the plant is deprived of atmospheric oxygen.", "The rate of photosynthesis decreases since the plant is deprived of atmospheric carbon dioxide.", "The rate of photosynthesis increases since the plant is getting enough amount of water.", "The rate of photosynthesis stays normal since the plant is getting water and sunlight."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q63", "text": "A plant is kept under green-colored light for an extended period of time. During this time, the plant is supplied by the suitable amount of CO2​ and water. How is photosynthesis affected under this condition?", "options": ["Photosynthesis increases since the green plants absorb green light only.", "Photosynthesis decreases since the green plants do not absorb green light.", "Photosynthesis increases since the green plants do not absorb green light.", "Photosynthesis will not be affected since the plant is supplied by the suitable amounts of water and CO2.", "Photosynthesis increases since the plant is supplied by the suitable amounts of water and CO2."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, 