s of photosynthesis are met."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q52", "text": "In a plant cell, if the Calvin cycle is disrupted, which process will be directly impacted?", "options": ["ATP synthesis", "Oxygen production", "Carbon fixation", "Water splitting", "Photophosphorylation"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q53", "text": "A student adds a chemical to a plant cell culture that inhibits the function of chloroplasts. What will be the immediate effect on the cells?", "options": ["A decrease in ATP production", "An increase in glucose production", "An increase in oxygen release", "An increase in carbon dioxide uptake", "An increase in starch storage"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q30", "text": "(Table) What can you conclude after studying the results shown in the table above? (Efficiency of photosynthesis vs. wavelength)", "options": ["The optimum wavelength for photosynthesis is between 400 and 600 nm.", "The optimum wavelength for photosynthesis is 650 nm.", "As the wavelength increases, the efficiency of photosynthesis continues to increase.", "As the wavelength increases, the efficiency of photosynthesis initially decreases before eventually increasing.", "The wavelength has no effect on photosynthesis efficiency."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 450 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"172\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wavelength (nm)</text>\n  <t