 A will increase since it has less CO₂, while plant B will undergo photosynthesis normally."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q29", "text": "Why light independent reaction cannot happen in dark?", "options": ["It depends on NADH and FADH2 produced by light reaction.", "It depends on NADH and ATP produced by light reaction.", "It depends on FADH2 and ATP produced by light reaction.", "It depends on NADPH and ATP produced by light reaction."], "answer": 3, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q32", "text": "Carotene is a pigment in carrots, and other vegetables that appear orange. What true about carotene?", "options": ["It strongly absorbs both blue-green and yellow-orange light", "It strongly absorbs blue-green light but does not strongly absorb yellow-orange color.", "It does not strongly absorb blue-green light but strongly absorbs yellow-orange light.", "It strongly absorbs neither blue-green nor yellow-orange light."], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q50", "text": "The Calvin cycle of photosynthesis takes place in:", "options": ["Stroma", "Thylakoid", "Vacuole", "Stomata"], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q62", "text": "There are membrane disk structures stacked on top of each other, and which are found in plastids.", "options": ["Stroma.", "Cristae", "Grana", "Leucoplasts"], "answer": 2, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q80", "text": "Which of the following is true regarding Photosynthesis?", "options": ["Light dependent reaction depends on the products from light independent reaction", "Light independent depends on the pr