xt>\n\n  <!-- Ticks -->\n  <text x=\"45\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text>\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">40</text>\n  <text x=\"245\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60</text>\n  <text x=\"310\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80</text>\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100</text>\n\n  <!-- Curve -->\n  <path d=\"M 45 135 Q 180 20 375 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0275d8\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"195\" cy=\"38\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#d9534f\"/>\n  <text x=\"195\" y=\"25\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#d9534f\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Optimum at Intermediate (~45 ppm)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q36", "text": "A scientist covered only the upper side of a plant's leaves with a transparent layer and kept the lower side intact. How would this affect the plant?", "options": ["The plant will not undergo photosynthesis.", "The rate of photosynthesis done by the plant will increase.", "The gas exchange through the stomata will stop since the upper side of the leaves has more stomata than the lower side.", "The gas exchange through the stomata will stop since the upper side of the leaves has fewer stomata than the lower side.", "The gas exchange through the stomata will barely decrease since the lower side of the leaves has more stomata than the upper side."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q39", "text": "Which of the following statements best describes the role of stomata?", "options": ["It absorbs sunlight.", "It is the site where photosynthesis occurs.", "It absorbs water and minerals from the soil.", "It is the site of the gas exchange.", "It transports sugars and minerals."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q10", "text": "A specific plant toxin often harms animal that eat the plant. Cell organelle that stores the toxin:", "options": ["chloroplast", "vacuole", "ribosome.", "Mitochondria"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q14", "text": "In vascular plants, which of the following terms best describe the structure of vascular system that transports sugar and other organic compounds through the plant?", "options": ["Phloem", "Xylem.", "Cambium.", "Pith."], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q56", "text": "The plant hormone responsible for fruit ripening is", "options": ["Ethylene", "Auxin", "Gibberellin", "Cytokinin"], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q60", "text": "Which property allows the interaction between water molecules in the xylem vessels of plants, contributing to their movement up these vessels?", "options": ["High heat capacity", "High heat of vaporization", "Cohesion", "Adhesion"], "answer": 2, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q89", "text": "What's common between the stomata in the lower dermis and alveoli in the lungs?", "options": ["Gas exchange", "ATP production", "Photosynthesis", "Cellular respiration"], "answer": 0, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q4", "text": "What is the advantage of having the feathery structure of the dandelion fruit?", "options": ["it helps evolve other species in other areas.", "it helps colonize habitats away from parent plant", "it gives sweet taste to the fruit", "it helps attract insects in order to increase pollination of the plant"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q29", "text": "Radish plants do not self-pollinate and rely mainly on insects to transferee pollen from plant to plant. which of the following structure that Reddish plant cannot produce on its own?", "options": ["Eggs.", "Flowers.", "Pollen.", "Seeds."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q61", "text": "Which of the following is asexual reproduction in plant?", "options": ["Formation of seeds", "Fusion between egg and sperm", "Cutting a part from coniferous tree and let it grow by itself.", "Ferns make spores"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q10", "text": "There is a plant in normal environment. Then we started to water it by salt water. After one week, what did turgid pressure in plant cells more likely to be lower or higher?", "options": ["turgid pressure will be higher because the plant cell will experience a net gain of water", "turgid pressure will be lower because the plant will experience a net loss of water", "turgid pressure will be higher because the plant will experience a net loss of water", "turgid pressure will be lower because the plant will experience a net gain of water"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q23", "text": "A certain plant stores toxic chemicals that, if ingested, are harmful to some animals. This toxic chemical is most likely stored in which of the following types of organelles?", "options": ["Vacuole", "Mitochondrion", "Ribosome", "Chloroplast"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q25", "text": "In vascular plants, which of the following best describes the component of the vascular system that transports sugars and organic nutrients throughout the plant?", "options": ["Cuticle", "Phloem", "Cortex", "Xylem"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q43", "text": "Given that radish plants do not self-pollinate and rely mainly on insects to transfer pollen from plant to plant, which of the following are radish plants unable to produce on their own?", "options": ["Eggs", "Flowers", "Pollen", "Seeds"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q53", "text": "Scientists have proposed the pressure-flow hypothesis to explain the transport of sugars within vascular plants. Which of the following types of tissue transports sugars in vascular plants?", "options": ["Collenchyma", "Phloem", "Parenchyma", "Xylem"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}]}, {"id": "cell-respiration", "title": "Cellular Respiration", "questions": [{"id": "est-old-1-q42", "text": "During glycolysis in cellular respiration, one molecule of glucose is broken down into", "options": ["alcohol.", "2 lactic acid molecules.", "3 lactic acid molecules.", "2 pyruvic acid molecules.", "3 pyruvic acid molecules."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q12", "text": "It occurs during strenuous exercise when the body cannot keep up with the demand of oxygen.", "options": ["Alcoholic fermentation", "Lactic acid fermentation", "Glycolysis", "Krebs cycle", "Calvin cycle"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q13", "text": "It occurs in the cytoplasm where one glucose molecule is broken apart into two molecules of pyruvate.", "options": ["Alcoholic fermentation", "Lactic acid fermentation", "Glycolysis", "Krebs cycle", "Calvin cycle"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q19", "text": "A phase of cellular respiration that occurs in the cristae of mitochondria is called", "options": ["glycolysis.", "the Krebs cycle.", "electron transport chain.", "the Calvin cycle.", "fermentation."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q76", "text": "The graph below shows the variation in the amount of oxygen used by the cell as a function of the intensity of exercise.Referring to the data from the above graph, we can conclude thatI. as the exercise becomes difficult, the body relies more on lactic acid fermentation.II. low intensity exercise does not require an increased oxygen uptake.III. difficult exercise requires additional oxygen in order to generate extra ATP for muscles.IV. during exercise, the body relies only on the aerobic pathway.", "options": ["I only", "III only", "I and II", "II and IV", "I, II and IV"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"320\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"450,247 458,250 450,253\" fill=\"#000000\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"77,30 80,22 83,30\" fill=\"#000000\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#e5e5e5\" stroke-width=\"0.8\">\n    <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"65\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"105\"/>\n    <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"145\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"145\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"185\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"185\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M 85 240 L 140 215 L 200 180 L 260 145 L 320 115 L 370 115 L 420 115\" \n        fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <g fil