"150\" y=\"208\" class=\"tgt\">Spermatogonia</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"222\" class=\"stat\" style=\"fill:#7a7263;\">Inactive</text>\n    <rect x=\"205\" y=\"190\" width=\"80\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F4F1E6\" stroke=\"#7a7263\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/>\n    <text x=\"245\" y=\"208\" class=\"tgt\">Sertoli cells</text>\n    <text x=\"245\" y=\"222\" class=\"stat\" style=\"fill:#7a7263;\">Not developed</text>\n  \n  <rect x=\"310\" y=\"0\" width=\"280\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#16232A\"/>\n  <text x=\"450\" y=\"20\" class=\"hdr\">Injection of FSH</text>\n  <rect x=\"380\" y=\"55\" width=\"140\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F4F1E6\" stroke=\"#16232A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"450\" y=\"79\" class=\"horm\">FSH hormone</text>\n<line x1=\"450\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"355\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#7a7263\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrG)\"/><line x1=\"450\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#3F7D5C\" stroke-width=\"2\"  marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/><line x1=\"450\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"545\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#3F7D5C\" stroke-width=\"2\"  marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n\n    <rect x=\"315\" y=\"190\" width=\"80\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F4F1E6\" stroke=\"#7a7263\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/>\n    <text x=\"355\" y=\"208\" class=\"tgt\">Leydig cells</text>\n    <text x=\"355\" y=\"222\" class=\"stat\" style=\"fill:#7a7263;\">Inactive</text>\n    <rect x=\"410\" y=\"190\" width=\"80\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F4F1E6\" stroke=\"#3F7D5C\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n    <text x=\"450\" y=\"208\" class=\"tgt\">Spermatogonia</text>\n    <text x=\"450\" y=\"222\" class=\"stat\" style=\"fill:#3F7D5C;\">Activated</text>\n    <rect x=\"505\" y=\"190\" width=\"80\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F4F1E6\" stroke=\"#3F7D5C\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n    <text x=\"545\" y=\"208\" class=\"tgt\">Sertoli cells</text>\n    <text x=\"545\" y=\"222\" class=\"stat\" style=\"fill:#3F7D5C;\">Developed</text>\n</svg>"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q9", "text": "Which system is responsible for the production of gametes and hormones that regulate sexual development and function?", "options": ["Reproductive system", "Endocrine system", "Nervous system", "Circulatory system"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q27", "text": "(Graphs) What conclusion can be derived from the values presented in the above graphs? (LH response)", "options": ["Estradiol provokes negative feedback on the pituitary gland, while estradiol along with progesterone provokes positive feedback.", "Estradiol alone does not affect pituitary gland secretion, but it provokes negative feedback when secreted with progesterone.", "Estradiol alone does not affect pituitary gland secretion, but it provokes positive feedback when secreted with progesterone.", "Estradiol provokes positive feedback on the pituitary gland, while estradiol along with progesterone provokes negative feedback.", "Estradiol and progesterone do not affect the pituitary gland."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph TD\n    Pituitary[\"Anterior Pituitary LH Secretion\"]\n    \n    E_alone[\"Estradiol alone\"] -->|Surge / Positive feedback| Pituitary\n    E_prog[\"Estradiol + Progesterone\"] -->|Inhibition / Negative feedback| Pituitary\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q23", "text": "Where does fertilization occur in human beings?", "options": ["Ovaries", "Uterus", "Vagina", "Endometrium", "Fallopian tubes"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q31", "text": "A 15-year-old girl suffers from delayed puberty... Which hormone is most likely to be the cause of her delayed puberty?", "options": ["Testosterone", "Thyroxine", "Estrogen", "Growth hormone", "LH"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q56", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be drawn from experiment 1? (Ablation of pituitary)", "options": ["The ovaries control the pituitary gland and the uterine cycle.", "The uterus controls the pituitary gland and the ovarian cycle.", "The absence of the pituitary gland maintains the ovarian and uterine cycles.", "The pituitary gland controls the size and cycles of the ovaries and uterus.", "The pituitary gland controls the cycle of the uterus only."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Pituitary[\"Anterior Pituitary\"] -->|Secretes FSH and LH| Ovaries[\"Ovaries\"]\n    Ovaries -->|Secretes Estrogen & Progesterone| Uterus[\"Uterus\"]\n    \n    subgraph Exp3 [\"Experiment 3 Proof\"]\n        OvariesBlocked[\"Ovaries Removed (X)\"] -.->|No estrogen/progesterone| UterineFailure[\"Uterine cycle fails despite FSH/LH\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q57", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be drawn from experiment 2? (Pituitary extracts FSH & LH)", "options": ["FSH and LH secreted by the pituitary gland maintain the size of the ovaries and the uterus, as well as their cycles.", "FSH and LH secreted by the pituitary gland maintain the size and cycle of the ovaries only.", "FSH and LH secreted by the pituitary gland maintain the size and cycle of the uterus only.", "The uterus stimulates the pituitary gland to secrete FSH and LH to maintain the size and cycle of the ovaries.", "The ovaries stimulate the pituitary gland to secrete FSH and LH to maintain the size and cycle of the uterus."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Pituitary[\"Anterior Pituitary\"] -->|Secretes FSH and LH| Ovaries[\"Ovaries\"]\n    Ovaries -->|Secretes Estrogen & Progesterone| Uterus[\"Uterus\"]\n    \n    subgraph Exp3 [\"Experiment 3 Proof\"]\n        OvariesBlocked[\"Ovaries Removed (X)\"] -.->|No estrogen/progesterone| UterineFailure[\"Uterine cycle fails despite FSH/LH\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q58", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be drawn from experiment 3? (Ovariectomized animals)", "options": ["The pituitary gland has no effect on the ovaries.", "The pituitary gland has no effect on the uterus.", "The pituitary gland controls the uterus indirectly through the ovaries.", "The pituitary gland controls the ovaries indirectly through the uterus.", "The ovaries control the pituitary gland, which in turn controls the uterus."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    Pituitary[\"Anterior Pituitary\"] -->|Secretes FSH and LH| Ovaries[\"Ovaries\"]\n    Ovaries -->|Secretes Estrogen & Progesterone| Uterus[\"Uterus\"]\n    \n    subgraph Exp3 [\"Experiment 3 Proof\"]\n        OvariesBlocked[\"Ovaries Removed (X)\"] -.->|No estrogen/progesterone| UterineFailure[\"Uterine cycle fails despite FSH/LH\"]\n    end\n"}, {"id": "act-3-q66", "text": "the ovum moves through the fallopian tube by the help of cells lining the fallopian tube. These cells must have which of the following structure to perform this action?", "options": ["Flagella", "Cilia", "Microvilli", "Pseudopods"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q89", "text": "which of the following produced by asexual reproduction?", "options": ["a pine tree that grew from a seed released from a pine cone.", "an aspen tree that grew by branching from roots of another aspen tree.", "a cherry tree that grew out of the waste of an animal that had eaten cherries.", "Zucchini plant that grew from a seed after pollination by an insect."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}]}, {"id": "animal-behavior", "title": "Animal Behavior", "questions": [{"id": "est-old-1-q32", "text": "A turtle draws its head back into its shell when its shell is touched. After being touched repeatedly, the turtle realizes it is not in danger and no longer hides. This is an example of", "options": ["courtship.", "circadian rhythm.", "imprinting.", "habituation.", "classical conditioning."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q39", "text": "A family moved to a new house by the train station. During the first few days, the sounds of the trains kept them awake. After that, the sounds of trains didn't wake them anymore. This is an example of", "options": ["operant conditioning.", "classical conditioning.", "insight learning.", "habituation.", "sensitization."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q59", "text": "The process by which a young animal learns to recognize and follow the first moving object is called", "options": ["imprinting.", "insight learning.", "habituation.", "classical conditioning.", "operant conditioning."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q72", "text": "On a chilly day, a (an) ________ moves from shade to a sunny rock.", "options": ["chordate", "vertebrate", "ectotherm", "endotherm", "mammal"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q5", "text": "Birds on the side of the road take flight when a car approaches. After many cars pass without harming the birds, the birds do not fly anymore when a car approaches. This is an example of", "options": ["classical conditioning.", "operant conditioning.", "imprinting.", "habituation.", "insight learning."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q26", "text": "Young birds follow the first moving object they see after they are born. This is known as", "options": ["classical conditioning.", "operant conditioning.", "imprinting.", "insight learning.", "habituation."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q62", "text": "The cockroach is an insect known for its rapid escape. In order to identify the stimulus that causes its escape and the sense organ that receives the stimulus; the following experiments were performed.Based on the above experiments, the stimulus that caused the cockroach to escape was", "options": ["seeing the predator.", "smelling the odor of the predator.", "feeling the air produced by the movement of the predator.", "hearing the voice of the predator.", "hearing the voice of the predator and feeling the air produced by the predator's movement."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 290\" width=\"100%\" height=\"290\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"25\" width=\"630\" height=\"240\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"215\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"215\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"265\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"265\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0f172a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"82\" y=\"49\">Experiment</text>\n    <text x=\"295\" y=\"49\">Experiment</text>\n    <text x=\"552\" y=\"49\">Result</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#0f172a\">\n    <text x=\"82\" y=\"93\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Experiment 1</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"85\">A cockroach was placed in a glass box with a</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"101\">speaker producing the voice of a toad.</text>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"85\">The cockroach didn't run</text>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"101\">away.</text>\n\n    <text x=\"82\" y=\"142\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Experiment 2</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"135\">A cockroach was placed alone in the glass box</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"151\">with air blowing on it.</text>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"142\">The cockroach ran away.</text>\n\n    <text x=\"82\" y=\"185\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Experiment 3</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"177\">The antennae of the cockroach were covered</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"193\">with petroleum based jelly, which acts as an</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"209\">insulator, then air is blown on the cockroach.</text>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"193\">The cockroach ran away.</text>\n\n    <text x=\"82\" y=\"238\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Experiment 4</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"233\">The legs of the cockroach were covered with</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"249\">petroleum based jelly, then air was blown on the</text>\n    <text x=\"150\" y=\"261\">cockroach.</text>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"238\">The cockroach didn't run</text>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"254\">away.</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-3-q15", "text": "A 7 year old student tends to complete his homework daily because he/she knows that he/she will be rewarded with candy. This is an example of", "options": ["insight learning.", "sensitization.", "habituation.", "operant conditioning.", "classical conditioning."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q13", "text": "Students who talk without raising their hands in class get sent to the principal's office.", "options": ["Habituation", "Operant conditioning", "Classical conditioning", "Imprinting", "Observational learning"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q14", "text": "Squirrels run away when a person wants to take a picture of them; however, after some trials, they do not mind staying close for a picture.", "options": ["Habituation", "Operant conditioning", "Classical conditioning", "Imprinting", "Observational learning"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q15", "text": "One macaque monkey washed a dirty potato in a nearby river; next, all the other monkeys did the same with their potatoes.", "options": ["Habituation", "Operant conditioning", "Classical conditioning", "Imprinting", "Observational learning"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q14", "text": "The Amur bitterling are fish that live in rivers. At the time of reproduction, the female develops a long tube called the egg-laying tube. When a male meets a female with this tube, he swims around her and guides her to a freshwater mussel... The nature of the stimulus is", "options": ["visual", "auditory", "olfactory", "gustatory", "both visual and auditory"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q71", "text": "Fixed action patterns are initiated by external stimuli called", "options": ["agonistic behavior.", "altruistic behavior.", "sign stimuli.", "associative learning.", "initial visual imprinting."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q75", "text": "Konrad Lorenz investigated a certain learning mechanism. He explains that it's learning that occurs during sensitive or critical periods in early life, and it cannot be reversed. He is referring to", "options": ["habituation.", "operant conditioning.", "trial and error learning.", "imprinting.", "classical conditioning."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-1-q24", "text": "The cycle of sleeping and waking up early every day is an example of", "options": ["courtship", "habituation", "imprinting", "circadian rhythm", "classical conditioning"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q48", "text": "A person who has lived in a rural area moved to a city... However, as time went on, he became accustomed to these stimuli and was able to sleep. This is an example of", "options": ["operant conditioning", "classical conditioning", "habituation", "imprinting", "insight learning"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q46", "text": "An individual suffered from vomiting and diarrhea after eating tuna. Since that day, every time he tastes tuna, he feels sick. This is an example of", "options": ["habituation", "operant conditioning", "classical conditioning", "imprinting", "insight learning"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q57", "text": "in nests of some birds, if eggs hatched little bird from different species. The mother bird throws it away from its babies. This behaviour is:", "options": ["learned, because its experience.", "learned, it does it out of experience.", "fixed action pattern, because its innate.", "fixed action pattern because of its experience."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q60", "text": "mouse in maze try to arrive to end point after go from the start point. which things must not be changed to arrive in shorter time next times?", "options": ["start point.", "end point", "the track.", "all of the above."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}]}, {"id": "animal-physio", "title": "Animal Physiology", "questions": [{"id": "est-old-1-q78", "text": "In order to study the effect of stress on the secretion of cortisol hormone, several experiments were done. Three lots of mice were subjected to different states of stress, whereby the level of stress that Lot 1 was subjected to was less than that of Lot 2, and that of Lot 2 was less than that of Lot 3. Then, the plasma concentration of Cortisol in these mice was measured; the results are shown in document 1.Moreover, the same experiment was performed on mice who were subjected to the ablation (removal) of their adrenal glands. The results of measurements revealed a very low concentration of plasma Cortisol in the three lots of mice.What conclusion can be derived from the above document?", "options": ["Adrenal glands secrete more Cortisol during stress.", "Adrenal glands secrete less Cortisol during stress.", "Cortisol secretion is not affected by stress.", "Absence of Adrenal glands increases Cortisol level.", "Absence of Adrenal glands does not affect Cortisol level."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"320\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"410\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"77,30 80,20 83,30\" fill=\"#000000\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\n    <text