": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-2-q36", "text": "Babies receive antibodies from their mothers through nursing. It's an example of", "options": ["active immunity", "inflammatory reaction", "passive immunity", "vaccination", "nonspecific immune reaction"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q26", "text": "What is the function of white blood cells?", "options": ["Carry oxygen", "Carry carbon dioxide", "Detoxify the blood.", "Fight infections."], "answer": 3, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-1-q83", "text": "Phagocytes and lymphocytes are types of", "options": ["Red blood cells", "White blood cells", "Platelets", "Plasma"], "answer": 1, "answerUncertain": false, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-2-q96", "text": "When bacteria, viruses invade human body, certain types of white blood cells can surround and engulf these invaders and eliminate them from body. Which cellular structure these white blood cells make these action possible?", "options": ["Cilium", "Flagellum", "Central vacuole", "Pseudopodium"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-3-q23", "text": "when a pathogen invades the body, certain white blood cells engulf the pathogen. Which of the following structures allow this process?", "options": ["Cilia", "central vacuole.", "pseudopods.", "wall."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q69", "text": "What cell type functions to eliminate infection in the human body?", "options": ["Muscle cells", "Skin cells", "Red blood cells", "White blood cells"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}]}], "estOldTests": [{"id": "est-old-1", "title": "EST (Old) 