-old-1-q6", "text": "An organism that has an allele for green eyes and an allele for brown eyes is", "options": ["homozygous.", "homologous.", "heterozygous.", "non-homologous.", "true breeding."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q7", "text": "The ________ of an allele is the number of times that the allele occurs in a gene pool compared with the number of times other alleles occur.", "options": ["gene pool", "single gene trait", "relative frequency", "speciation", "directional selection"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q8", "text": "The following graph shows the rate of photosynthesis in sun plants and shade plants as a function of intensity of light.Which statement best describes the conclusion drawn from of the above figure?\nI. In shade plants, the rate of photosynthesis increases at a low intensity of light and is not affected when the intensity of light increases.\nII. In both kinds of plants, the rate of photosynthesis increases as the intensity of light increases.\nIII. In sun plants, the rate of photosynthesis increases as the intensity of light increases.\nIV. In shade plants, the rate of photosynthesis is not affected by light.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "III only", "I and III", "III and IV"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 350\" width=\"100%\" height=\"350\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <defs>\n    <pattern id=\"grid8\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\">\n      <path d=\"M 25 0 L 0 0 0 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#dcdcdc\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/>\n    </pattern>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"40\" width=\"375\" height=\"220\" fill=\"url(#grid8)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"470\" y