logous structure.", "natural selection.", "adaptation."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q12", "text": "Traits controlled by more than one gene are", "options": ["codominant.", "incomplete dominant.", "dominant.", "multiple alleles.", "polygenic."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q13", "text": "Bryophytes transport water by", "options": ["active transport.", "vascular tissue.", "osmosis.", "transpiration.", "evaporation."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q14", "text": "After mating a black guinea pig and a white guinea pig, all offspring obtained were black. Which conclusion can be drawn from this cross?", "options": ["This trait is a single gene trait.", "This trait is a polygenic trait.", "This is a sex linked trait.", "This is codominant inheritance.", "This is intermediate dominant inheritance."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q15", "text": "The following figure shows the amount of precipitation and variation of temperature in Belem, Brazil throughout a year.To which Biome does Belem belong?", "options": ["Desert", "Tropical rain forest", "Temperate grassland", "Tropical dry forest", "Temperate woodland"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 550 360\" width=\"100%\" height=\"360\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"470\" y1=\"280\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5