ll.II. the size of prokaryotic cells is bigger than the size of a eukaryotic cell.III. the size of all human cells is bigger than the size of any other eukaryotic cell.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "III only", "I and III", "II and III"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": "Yes (Table)"}, {"id": "est-old-1-q18", "text": "Members of two different species are unable to interbreed and produce fertile offspring due to barriers. This is called the mechanism of", "options": ["genetic equilibrium.", "genetic drift.", "temporal isolation.", "mutation.", "reproductive isolation."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q19", "text": "Sections of RNA that are removed after transcription are", "options": ["exons.", "introns.", "codon.", "promoters.", "anti-codon."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q20", "text": "The small dense region inside the nucleus that is responsible for the synthesis of ribosomes is the", "options": ["Golgi body.", "rough endoplasmic reticulum.", "smooth endoplasmic reticulum.", "nucleolus.", "mitochondria."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q21", "text": "A road built through a forest splits a population of frogs into two large groups. The allele frequencies of these two groups stayed identical. What conclusion can be drawn?", "options": ["This road caused a bottleneck effect.", "This road caused a founder effect.", "This road didn't cause a genetic drift.", "This road caused a disruptive selection.", "This road caused a directional selection."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q22", "text": "One of the daughter cells obtained by the end of a mitotic division contains 12 chromosomes. Therefore, the number of chromosomes in the initial cell is", "options": ["24 chromosomes.", "12 chromosomes.", "42 chromosomes.", "36 chromosomes.", "46 chromosomes."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q23", "text": "________ is a process by which plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to create oxygen and energy in the form of sugar.", "options": ["Fermentation", "Glycolysis", "Chemosynthesis", "Photosynthesis", "Krebs cycle"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q24", "text": "The following graph shows the average heart rate, with respect to plasma morphine concentration.What conclusion can be drawn concerning the effect of morphine on heart rate?", "options": ["As morphine concentration increases, heart rate decreases.", "As morphine concentration increases, heart rate increases.", "Morphine has no effect on heart rate.", "Heart rate decreases the most at 10 ng/mL of morphine concentration.", "Heart rate decreases the least at 70 ng/mL of morphine concentration."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 500 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"320\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"end\">\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"55\">80</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"80\">70</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"105\">60</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"130\">50</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"155\">40</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"180\">30</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"205\">20</text>\n    <text x=\"62\" y=\"230\">10</text>