eral days?", "options": ["The rate of photosynthesis increases since the plant is exposed to light for a long period of time.", "The rate of photosynthesis decreases since the plant is deprived of atmospheric oxygen.", "The rate of photosynthesis decreases since the plant is deprived of atmospheric carbon dioxide.", "The rate of photosynthesis increases since the plant is getting enough amount of water.", "The rate of photosynthesis stays normal since the plant is getting water and sunlight."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q26", "text": "A farmer breeds two plants to produce new plants with specific traits. This is an example of", "options": ["natural selection.", "common descent.", "natural variation.", "artificial selection.", "adaptation."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q27", "text": "________ is a specialized vascular tissue that transports nutrients and carbohydrates in plants.", "options": ["Tracheid", "Xylem", "Sporophyte", "Vein", "Phloem"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q28", "text": "Upon crossing a male rabbit having Bb genotype with a female rabbit having Bb genotype, the offspring obtained have genotypes with ratios of 2/3 Bb and 1/3 bb (it is a case of dominance inheritance with B as the dominant allele and b as the recessive allele). What can you conclude from this cross?", "options": ["Allele b is lethal allele.", "Allele B is lethal allele.", "Presence of allele B with allele b is lethal.", "Both alleles B and b are lethal.", "Individuals with pure genotypes do not survive."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q29", "text": "The following diagram shows the average age of males and females in the Rwandan population.Which s