, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q38", "text": "A plant having genotype TT is crossed with another plant having genotype Tt (T is the symbol of the dominant allele, and t is the symbol of the recessive allele). Which statement is true concerning the offspring that result from this cross?", "options": ["All offspring will have the dominant character as a phenotype.", "All offspring will have the recessive character as a phenotype.", "75% of the offspring will have the dominant character as a phenotype, and 25% will have the recessive character.", "25% of the offspring will have the dominant character as a phenotype, and 75% will have the recessive character.", "50% of the offspring will have the dominant character as a phenotype, and 50% will have the recessive character."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q39", "text": "A family moved to a new house by the train station. During the first few days, the sounds of the trains kept them awake. After that, the sounds of trains didn't wake them anymore. This is an example of", "options": ["operant conditioning.", "classical conditioning.", "insight learning.", "habituation.", "sensitization."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q40", "text": "A scientist measured the pH of water in a small pond at several intervals throughout the day. The results are represented in the following figure.What can you conclude concerning the variation of pH in the pond?I. pH rises with increasing daylight and falls with decreasing daylight.II. pH decreases with increasing daylight and increases with decreasing daylight.\nIII. The pond is least acidic from midnight till 6 am.\nIV. The pond is most acidic from midnight till 6 am.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "III only", "I and III", "I and IV"], "answer": 4, "e