stion of food ends in the stomach.", "Yes, since absorption of food occurs in the large intestine."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q58", "text": "Two long pea plants are crossed with each other. 3/4 of the plants obtained from this cross peas are long, and 1/4 of the plants peas are short. We can conclude thatI. long plants that are crossed with each other are hybrid.II. long plants that are crossed with each other are pure.III. allele long is dominant over allele short.IV. allele short is dominant over allele long.", "options": ["III only", "I and III", "I and IV", "II and III", "II and IV"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q59", "text": "The process by which a young animal learns to recognize and follow the first moving object is called", "options": ["imprinting.", "insight learning.", "habituation.", "classical conditioning.", "operant conditioning."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q60", "text": "Which of the following occurs during prophase of mitosis?\nI. Chromosomes line up at the middle of the cell.\nII. Centrioles change into asters and spindle fibers appear.\nIII. The cytoplasm divides.\nIV. The nuclear membrane disappears.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "III only", "II and III", "II and IV"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q61", "text": "A study was done in order to monitor the effect of tobacco on respiration. The amounts of oxygen, O2​, and carbon monoxide, CO, were measured in blood leaving the lungs of smokers and nonsmokers, and the results are shown in the table below.What can you conclude concerning the effect of tobacco on the formation of oxyhemoglobin HbO2​ and HbCO?\nI. Tobacco has no effect on the formation of HbO2​ and HbCO.\nII. Tobacco increases the formation of HbO2​.\nIII. Tobacco decreases the formation of HbO2​.\nIV. Tobacco increases the formation of HbCO.\nV. Tobacco decreases the formation of HbCO.", "options": ["I only", "II and IV", "II and V", "III and IV", "III and V"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": "Yes (Table)"}, {"id": "est-old-1-q62", "text": "Individuals with multiple sclerosis have their immune system attack the myelin sheath of the neurons found in the central nervous system. How would damage to the myelin sheath affect the transmission of nervous messages?", "options": ["Nervous messages would be transmitted normally since the neurons are not destroyed.", "Nervous messages would be transmitted faster since the presence of myelin sheath decreases the speed of the nervous message.", "Nervous messages would be transmitted slower since the presence of myelin sheath increases the speed of the nervous message.", "The transmission of nervous messages would start at a fast speed and then decrease.", "The transmission of nervous messages would start at a slow speed and then increase."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q63", "text": "A plant is kept under green-colored light for an extended period of time. During this time, the plant is supplied by the suitable amount of CO2​ and water. How is photosynthesis affected under this condition?", "options": ["Photosynthesis increases since the green plants absorb green light only.", "Photosynthesis decreases since the green plants do not absorb green light.", "Photosynthesis increases since the green plants do not absorb green light.", "Photosynthesis will not be affected since the plant is supplied by the suitable amounts of water and CO2.", "Photosynthesis increases since the plant is supplied by the suitable amounts of water and CO2."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q64", "text": "How many mitotic divisions does a cell undergo to produce a tissue of 64 cells?", "options": ["5 divisions", "4 divisions", "2 divisions", "6 divisions", "7 divisions"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q65", "text": "The amount of mitochondria as a percentage of total cell volume is measured in the atria and ventricles of the heart. The amount of mitochondria present in the cells of the left ventricle is 49%, while that in the cells of the left atrium is 35%. How can you explain the difference in the amount of mitochondria in atria and ventricles?\nI. The size of atrium is smaller than the size of ventricles.\nII. The atrium pumps blood a very short distance, while the ventricle pumps blood a long distance.\nIII. The atrium needs less force to pump blood than the ventricle.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "I and II", "II and III", "I, II and III"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q66", "text": "What is the role of cyclin?", "options": ["It regulates the timing of the cell cycle.", "It is responsible for the formation of ribosomes.", "It activates cytokinesis.", "It is responsible for the formation of spindle fibers.", "It is responsible for the duplication of chromosomes."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q67", "text": "Crossing over may occur during", "options": ["anaphase I.", "anaphase II.", "prophase I.", "prophase II.", "metaphase II."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q68", "text": "The primary role of yellow bone marrow and the reason it is yellow is", "options": ["to produce white blood cells.", "to produce red blood cells.", "to produce plasma.", "to store calcium.", "to store fats."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-1-q69", "text": "The following table shows the number of births over deaths in a population from 1900 to 1990.The above study shows", "options": ["exponential growth since the number of births over deaths decreased.", "logistic growth since the number of births over deaths decreased.", "exponential growth since the number of births over deaths increased.", "logistic growth since the number of births over deaths increased.", "what starts as exponential growth and continues as logistic growth."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": "Yes (Table)"}, {"id": "est-old-1-q70", "text": "Examine the following cladogram.What conclusion can be drawn from the above cladogram?", "options": ["Organisms X and Y have a most recent common ancestor.", "Organisms X and Z have a most recent common ancestor.", "Organisms Y and Z have a most recent common ancestor.", "Organisms X and Y have common ancestor, but organism Z doesn't have the same ancestor as X and Y.", "None of these organisms have a common ancestor."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 1", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 240\" width=\"100%\" height=\"240\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <line x1=\"160\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <line x1=\"210\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <line x1=\"210\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <line x1=\"150\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <line x1=\"150\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"50\