\"/>\n      <ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#22c55e\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\"/>\n      <ellipse cx=\"15\" cy=\"-25\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#22c55e\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(-120)\"/>\n      <ellipse cx=\"25\" cy=\"-5\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#22c55e\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(-150)\"/>\n    </g>\n    <text x=\"45\" y=\"130\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">G</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-2-q74", "text": "To prove that DNA replication is semi-conservative, an experiment was done on Lily roots. A lily root cell containing DNA labeled with heavy nitrogen (N15) is placed in a medium containing light nitrogen (N14) and is allowed to make 2 consecutive cell cycles. The number of cells containing only light nitrogen (N14) at the end of 2 consecutive cell cycles is", "options": ["2 cells.", "4 cells.", "8 cells.", "16 cells.", "32 cells."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-2-q75", "text": "The following figure shows a beaker containing water and solute separated by a selectively permeable membrane. What would happen after a few minutes?", "options": ["Osmosis of water from medium 1 to medium 2 would take place.", "Diffusion of the solute from medium 1 to medium 2 would take place.", "Osmosis of water from medium 2 to medium 1 would take place.", "Diffusion of the solute from medium 2 to medium 1 would take place.", "Nothing changes."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 2", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 280\" width=\"100%\" height=\"280\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"40\" width=\"260\" height=\"180\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#000