te of photosynthesis by green plants.", "Loss of species diversity due to loss of habitat.", "An increase in global water temperature that negatively affects aquatic animals."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q75", "text": "When cells acquire specialized features during embryonic development, it is called", "options": ["metamorphosis.", "differentiation.", "mutation.", "evolution.", "embryology."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q76", "text": "Mitral valve regurgitation is a heart condition where the mitral valve does not close completely... Which chamber of the heart is the blood abnormally leaking to?", "options": ["Right atrium", "Left atrium", "Right ventricle", "Left ventricle", "It cannot be determined."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q77", "text": "Increased levels of nitrates and phosphates in a body of water cause a drastic increase in the aquatic plant life. This is an example of", "options": ["mutualism.", "eutrophication.", "primary succession.", "nitrogen fixation.", "logistic growth."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q78", "text": "Which of the following shows the correct order of the Linnaean taxonomic ranks?", "options": ["Order, family, genus", "Phylum, order, class", "Kingdom, class, phylum", "Family, class, phylum", "Genus, species, family"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-4-q79", "text": "Organism X has the diploid number of chromosomes 2N=24. How many chromosomes does organism's sperm contain?", "options": ["24", "12", "48", "6", "It differs from one sperm to another."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 4", "hasVisual": 