", "options": ["7%", "50%", "60%", "81%", "91%"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q6", "text": "If the climate were to change so that snow covered the ground much of the time, what change in the population of foxes would you expect?", "options": ["The frequency of white allele would increase.", "The frequency of white allele would decrease.", "The frequency of red allele would increase.", "The population of foxes would decrease and then increase.", "The population of foxes would increase and then decrease."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q7", "text": "In the ABO blood group system, the alleles behave as follows:", "options": ["IAIA is the genotype of group A, which is homozygous.", "IBIB is the genotype of group A which is heterozygous.", "IAi is the genotype of group A which is homozygous.", "The two alleles IA and i are codominant.", "Allele IA is dominant over allele IB."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q8", "text": "Red blood cells are placed in three solutions of different concentrations. The microscopic observations of these cells are done, and the results are shown in the following table.Consider that the cytoplasm of red blood cells has a concentration of 9 grams/100cc. Which statement is INCORRECT?", "options": ["The red blood cells lyse in solution 1 because the water passes by osmosis from the exterior hypotonic medium into the interior hypertonic medium.", "The red blood cells lyse because the cytoplasmic concentration is less than that of solution 1, thus leading to enormous turgidity.", "The red blood cells remain normal in solution 2 because both the intracellular and extracellular media are isotonic.", "The red blood cells shrink because water exits from the hypotonic medium to the hypertonic medium by plasmolysis in solution 3.", "The red blood cells don't lyse because there is no exchange that occurs between the two media in solution 2."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"630\" height=\"135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"220\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"365\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"365\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <line x1=\"510\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"510\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0f172a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"122\" y=\"47\">Solution number</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"47\">1</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"47\">2</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"47\">3</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#0f172a\">\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"85\" font-weight=\"bold\">Concentration of the</text>\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"99\" font-weight=\"bold\">solution in % (g/cc)</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.03</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.09</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\">26</text>\n\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"130\" font-weight=\"bold\">Aspect of red blood</text>\n    <text x=\"35\" y=\"145\" font-weight=\"bold\">cells</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red blood cells</text>\n    <text x=\"292\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bulge and lyse</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red blood cells</text>\n    <text x=\"437\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\">remain normal</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Red blood cells</text>\n    <text x=\"582\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\">shrink</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-old-5-q9", "text": "The complete cardiac cycle involves three phases: the auricular systole, the ventricular systole, and the general diastole.Which is the correct statement?", "options": ["During the auricular systole, blood leaves the auricles by the arteries.", "During the ventricular systole, blood leaves the ventricles by the veins.", "During the general diastole, blood comes back to the auricles by the veins.", "During the general diastole, blood comes back to the auricles by the arteries.", "During the ventricular systole, atrioventricular valves are opened."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q10", "text": "A biology class was performing an experiment in the lab. The students had obtained a DNA strand with radioactive thymine. Later, as they left the strand in a medium for multiplication, they realized that the radioactivity was observed only in part of the DNA and not all DNA molecules.  The process was explained by the teacher as", "options": ["DNA translation.", "cell proliferation.", "semi-conservative replication of DNA.", "conservative replication of DNA.", "semi-conservative translation of DNA."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q11", "text": "In which leaf/leaves is the blue color seen only in the central region as the result of the iodine test?", "options": ["Leaf 1", "Leaf 2", "Leaf 3", "Leaf 3 and 4", "Leaf 2 and 4"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"