: "The Amur bitterling are fish that live in rivers. At the time of reproduction, the female develops a long tube called the egg-laying tube. When a male meets a female with this tube, he swims around her and guides her to a freshwater mussel... The nature of the stimulus is", "options": ["visual", "auditory", "olfactory", "gustatory", "both visual and auditory"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q15", "text": "Which of the following is LEAST likely to result in speciation?", "options": ["random mating among members of a large population of a species", "occurrence of hybridization between individuals from two different species", "development of different mating behavior by some members of a species", "emigration to a specialized microenvironment by some members of a species", "formation of a physical barrier that blocks gene flow between members of a species"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-old-5-q16", "text": "The following table shows the results of an experiment made in order to test the duration of seed germination as a function of temperature.On the basis of the data above, a temperature of", "options": ["20∘C allows for very fast development.", "35∘C maximally slows down seed germination.", "25∘C allows for very fast development.", "8∘C allows for very fast development.", "12∘C maximally slows down seed germination."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST Old 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 150\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\">\n  <rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n  <rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"630\" height=\"105\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"655\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"2