al": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q47", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. The allele frequency of dominant brown lentils is", "options": ["0.3", "0.245", "0.49", "0.7", "0.07"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q48", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. The allele frequency of recessive red lentils is", "options": ["0.51", "0.3", "0.03", "0.42", "0.755"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q49", "text": "On a population of lentils at equilibrium, the brown lentil allele is dominant over the red lentil allele. The probability of homozygous brown is 0.49. The probability of individuals to be heterozygote is", "options": ["0.21", "0.088", "0.42", "0.044", "0.9"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q50", "text": "If a cell's mitochondrial DNA is damaged, which cellular process would be directly affected?", "options": ["Protein synthesis", "Lipid synthesis", "Cellular respiration", "DNA replication", "Cell division"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q51", "text": "An inhibitor that blocks the active site of an enzyme involved in glycolysis is introduced to a cell. What is the most likely immediate effect?", "options": ["Increased production of ATP", "Accumulation of lipids", "Decreased production of pyruvate", "Increased oxygen consumption", "Decreased production of lactate"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q52", "text": "In a plant cell, if the Calvin cycle is disrupted, which process will be directly impacted?", "options": ["ATP synthesis", "Oxygen production", "Carbon fixation", "Water splitting", "Photophosphorylation"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q53", "text": "A student adds a chemical to a plant cell culture that inhibits the function of chloroplasts. What will be the immediate effect on the cells?", "options": ["A decrease in ATP production", "An increase in glucose production", "An increase in oxygen release", "An increase in carbon dioxide uptake", "An increase in starch storage"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-3-q54", "text": "(Graph) The relationship between the substrate concentration and the enzyme activity can be described as follows:", "options": ["The activity of the enzyme is independent of the substrate concentration.", "The activity of the enzyme continues to increase with the increase in the substrate concentration.", "The activity of the enzyme decreases with the increase in the substrate concentration.", "As the substrate concentration increases to a certain value, the activity of the enzyme increases, and then it remains constant as the substrate concentration increases.", "As the substrate concentration increases to a certain value, the activity of the enzyme decreases, and then it remains constant as the substrate concentration increases."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 3", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 170\" width=\"100%\" height=\"170\">\n  <line x1=\"50\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"50\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"220\" y=\"162\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\