 Pattern\"}\n    Step4 -->|Main vein in middle| Magnolia[\"Magnolia\"]\n    Step4 -->|Branch from 1 point| Step5{\"Leaf Shape\"}\n    Step5 -->|Heart-shaped| Redbud[\"Redbud\"]\n    Step5 -->|Star-shaped| SweetGum[\"Sweet gum (Not listed -> E)\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q21", "text": "The division of the cytoplasm during cell division occurs during", "options": ["prophase", "cytokinesis", "anaphase", "telophase", "metaphase"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q22", "text": "(Cell Diagram) Which phase of mitosis does the above figure represent?", "options": ["Prophase", "Metaphase", "Anaphase", "Telophase", "Cytokinesis"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    G2[\"Parent Cell (2n = 6 duplicated chromosomes)\"] --> M[\"Metaphase (6 chromosomes at equator)\"]\n    M --> A[\"Anaphase Figure shown:<br>6 chromatids pulled to North pole<br>6 chromatids pulled to South pole\"]\n    A --> D[\"Daughter Cells (6 chromosomes each)\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q23", "text": "(Cell Diagram) Referring to the above figure, how many chromosomes did the initial cell have before it started the division?", "options": ["3 chromosomes", "6 chromosomes", "12 chromosomes", "23 chromosomes", "46 chromosomes"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    G2[\"Parent Cell (2n = 6 duplicated chromosomes)\"] --> M[\"Metaphase (6 chromosomes at equator)\"]\n    M --> A[\"Anaphase Figure shown:<br>6 chromatids pulled to North pole<br>6 chromatids pulled to South pole\"]\n    A --> D[\"Daughter Cells (6 chromosomes each)\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q24", "text": "(Graph) The relationship between ladybirds and aphids shown in Aphids the adjacent graph represents", "options": ["parasitism", "mutualism", "predator- prey relationship", "heterotrophy", "commensalism"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 450 190\" width=\"100%\" height=\"190\">\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"180\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Time</text>\n  <text x=\"-90\" y=\"18\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Number of organisms</text>\n\n  <!-- Aphids (Prey) Curve -->\n  <path d=\"M 40 120 Q 90 20 140 120 Q 190 160 240 120 Q 290 20 340 120 Q 380 160 410 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" font-weight=\"bold\">Aphids (Prey)</text>\n\n  <!-- Ladybirds (Predator) Curve: Lagging -->\n  <path d=\"M 40 150 Q 120 30 170 145 Q 220 160 270 145 Q 320 30 370 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c62828\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#c62828\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ladybirds (Predator)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q25", "text": "Body organs belonging to different organisms that perform similar functions but have different structures are known as", "options": ["analogous structures", "homologous structures", "vestigial organs", "acquired structures", "fossils"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q26", "text": "Which of the following hormones is NOT secreted by the anterior pituitary gland?", "options": ["FSH", "LH", "GH", "GnRH", "TSH"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q27", "text": "(Graphs) What conclusion can be derived from the values presented in the above graphs? (LH response)", "options": ["Estradiol provokes negative feedback on the pituitary gland, while estradiol along with progesterone provokes positive feedback.", "Estradiol alone does not affect pituitary gland secretion, but it provokes negative feedback when secreted with progesterone.", "Estradiol alone does not affect pituitary gland secretion, but it provokes positive feedback when secreted with progesterone.", "Estradiol provokes positive feedback on the pituitary gland, while estradiol along with progesterone provokes negative feedback.", "Estradiol and progesterone do not affect the pituitary gland."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph TD\n    Pituitary[\"Anterior Pituitary LH Secretion\"]\n    \n    E_alone[\"Estradiol alone\"] -->|Surge / Positive feedback| Pituitary\n    E_prog[\"Estradiol + Progesterone\"] -->|Inhibition / Negative feedback| Pituitary\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q28", "text": "Individuals who have their gall bladder removed because of gallstones would have difficulty digesting", "options": ["starch", "proteins", "fibers", "lipids", "starch and proteins"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q29", "text": "Which of the following nutrients does NOT enter the atmosphere during its cycle?", "options": ["Carbon", "Nitrogen", "Phosphorus", "Carbon and nitrogen", "Nitrogen and phosphorus"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-4-q30", "text": "(Table) What can you conclude after studying the results shown in the table above? (Efficiency of photosynthesis vs. wavelength)", "options": ["The optimum wavelength for photosynthesis is between 400 and 600 nm.", "The optimum wavelength for photosynthesis is 650 nm.", "As the wavelength increases, the efficiency of ph