e intensity of light increases above 200 µmol photon/m²/s.", "The rate of photosynthesis is best at the intensity of light 200 µmol photon/m²/s.", "The rate of photosynthesis increases gradually when the intensity of light ranges between 200 and 400 µmol photon/m²/s, and it increases sharply when the intensity of light ranges between 400 and 1000 µmol photon/m²/s.", "The rate of photosynthesis increases sharply when the intensity of light ranges between 200 and 400 µmol photon/m²/s, and it increases gradually when the intensity of light ranges between 400 and 1000 µmol photon/m²/s.", "The rate of photosynthesis and the intensity of light are not related."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"215\" y=\"172\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Light intensity (µmol photon/m²/s)</text>\n  <text x=\"-85\" y=\"18\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CO₂ absorbed</text>\n\n  <polyline points=\"45,150 110,95 180,35 250,27 320,20 380,20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"55\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" font-weight=\"bold\">Steep rise (200-400)</text>\n  <text x=\"290\" y=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#2e7d32\">Gradual plateau (400-1000)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-4-q38", "text": "During an experiment, a student observes a cell where all chromosomes are lined up at the center of the cell. Based on this information, which stage of cell cycle is the cell most likely in?", "options": ["Prophase", "Anaphase", "Interphase", 