172\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30</text>\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">45</text>\n\n  <!-- Inverted Parabola Curve -->\n  <path d=\"M 50 160 Q 220 20 390 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#d9534f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"220\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#d9534f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Peak: 20°C - 25°C</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q21", "text": "(Table) What conclusion can be drawn concerning the length of the life cycle of the plant cell?", "options": ["The cell cycle is fastest when the environmental temperature is 10°C.", "The cell cycle is fastest when the environmental temperature ranges between 10°C and 12°C.", "The cell cycle becomes slower as the temperature increases.", "The cell cycle becomes faster as the temperature increases.", "Environmental temperature has no effect on the duration of the cell cycle."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    T1[\"10°C: 70.2 hours (Slow)\"] --> T2[\"14°C: 62.0 hours\"]\n    T2 --> T3[\"18°C: 50.2 hours (Fastest)\"]\n    T1 & T2 & T3 --> Trend[\"Conclusion: Duration decreases / Cell cycle accelerates as temperature rises\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q22", "text": "A group of individuals belonging to the same species and living together in the same area is called", "options": ["a community", "a species", "an ecosystem", "a symbiosis", "a population"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q23", "text": "Where does fertilization occur in human beings?", "options": ["Ovaries", "Uterus", "Vagina", "Endometrium", "Fallopian tubes"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q24", "text": "(Graph) What conclusion can be drawn from the data? (Gibberellin vs. seed germination)", "options": ["The maximum rate is reached at a hormone concentration of 60 ppm.", "Seed germination is unaffected by the hormone concentration.", "Lower concentrations of the hormone promote seed germination.", "Intermediate concentrations of the hormone yield the lowest germination rates.", "Intermediate concentrations of the hormone yield the highest germination rates."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 180\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\">\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"45\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"220\" y=\"172\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gibberellin Concentration (ppm)</text>\n  <text x=\"-85\" y=\"16\" transform=\"rotate(-90)\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Germination Rate (%)</text>\n\n  <!-- Ticks -->\n  <text x=\"45\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text>\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">40</text>\n  <text x=\"245\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">60</text>\n  <text x=\"310\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80</text>\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100</text>\n\n  <!-- Curve -->\n  <path d=\"M 45 135 Q 180 20 375 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0275d8\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"195\" cy=\"38\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#d9534f\"/>\n  <text x=\"195\" y=\"25\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#d9534f\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Optimum at Intermediate (~45 ppm)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q25", "text": "(Table) What is the relation between smoking cigarettes and atherosclerosis?", "options": ["The risk of developing atherosclerosis is lowest when more than 20 cigarettes are smoked per day.", "The risk of developing atherosclerosis is highest when 10-19 cigarettes are smoked per day.", "As the number of smoked cigarettes increases, the risk of developing atherosclerosis increases.", "As the number of smoked cigarettes decreases, the risk of developing atherosclerosis increases.", "The risk of atherosclerosis remains constant regardless of smoking habits."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    C0[\"0 cigarettes: 1.0%\"] --> C1[\"1-9 cigarettes: 1.5%\"]\n    C1 --> C2[\"10-19 cigarettes: 2.0%\"]\n    C2 --> C3[\"> 20 cigarettes: 2.5%\"]\n    C0 & C1 & C2 & C3 --> Trend[\"Direct positive correlation: Higher consumption -> Higher risk\"]\n"}, {"id": "est-new-5-q26", "text": "Which of the following is an example of mutualism?", "options": ["A lion hunting a zebra", "A bee pollinating a flower", "A flea living on a dog", "A hawk eating a mouse", "A tree shading a smaller plant"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q27", "text": "Which of the following is true about crossing over?", "options": ["Crossing over occurs between sister chromatids.", "Crossing over leads to increased genetic diversity.", "Crossing over reduces genetic variation.", "Crossing over only occurs in meiosis II.", "Crossing over results in identical daughter cells."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q28", "text": "The scientific names of the domestic cat and the wildcat are Felis catus and Felis silvestris, respectively. These animals are classified under", "options": ["the same genus", "the same species", "the same species and kingdom", "the same species and genus", "the same species and family"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q29", "text": "(DNA Fingerprint) Draw out a conclusion concerning the dominant allele. (Galactosemia)", "options": ["The normal allele is dominant since the mother has a mutant allele and a normal allele, but only the normal allele is expressed.", "The mutant allele is dominant since the mother has a mutant allele and a normal allele, but only the mutant allele is expressed.", "The mutant allele is dominant since the normal mother has a mutant allele, but it was not expressed.", "The normal allele is dominant since the normal father has 2 normal alleles.", "The normal allele and the mutant allele are codominant since the mother and the fetus have normal and mutant alleles."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 380 160\" width=\"100%\" height=\"160\">\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"360\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#f8f9fa\" stroke=\"#ccc\" rx=\"4\"/>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mother</text>\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Father</text>\n  <text x=\"310\" y=\"32\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fetus</text>\n\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"65\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#444\">Normal allele</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"115\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#444\">Mutant allele</text>\n\n  <!-- Mother bands -->\n  <rect x=\"85\" y=\"55\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#222\" rx=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"85\" y=\"105\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#222\" rx=\"2\"/>\n\n  <!-- Father bands -->\n  <rect x=\"185\" 