swer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q47", "text": "An individual consumed a meal consisting of 10 g of carbohydrates, 20 g of proteins, and 5 g of lipids... What is the total energy obtained from this meal?", "options": ["17 kcal", "35 kcal", "85 kcal", "155 kcal", "165 kcal"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q48", "text": "The energy produced by a plant in a food chain is 150 calories. What amount of energy would be available for the 2ⁿᵈ level consumer?", "options": ["0.15 calories", "1.5 calories", "15 calories", "150 calories", "1500 calories"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q49", "text": "Adult tapeworms are long flatworms that live in the intestines of humans... This is an example of", "options": ["predator prey relationship", "parasitic symbiosis", "mutualistic symbiosis", "commensalism", "carrying capacity"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "est-new-5-q50", "text": "(Graph) What conclusion can be drawn from the information presented in the above graph? (Ice melting in Antarctica)", "options": ["The maximum amount of ice melting was between 1994 and 2000.", "The maximum amount of ice melting was between 2008 and 2016.", "The maximum amount of ice melting was between 2000 and 2006.", "The maximum amount of ice melting was between 1996 and 2002.", "The maximum amount of ice melting was between 1998 and 2004."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "", "source": "EST New 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualMermaid": "graph LR\n    P1[\"1994 to 2000:<br>Modest decline (-500 Gt)\"] --> P2[\"2000 to 2008:<br>Steady melt (-1000 Gt)\"]\n    P2 --> P3[\"2008 to 2016:<br>Steepest plunge (-1500 Gt drop)\"]\n    P3 --> Conclusion[\"Conclusion: Maximum amount of