rently shaped dorsal lines would indicate the 2 species inherited the lines from a common ancestor", "yes, their similarity in structure indicates the two species have a common ancestor", "yes, the two species that exist in similar environment must have inherited the trait from a common ancestor"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q6", "text": "What must occur for two species to be considered different species? I. they should be geographically isolated. II. they should be reproductively isolated. III. They should share same ecological niche.", "options": ["I only", "II only", "I and II only", "I, II, III"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q7", "text": "Which of the following process need ATP? I) contraction of cardiac muscle. II) movement of molecules against concentration gradient. III) CO2 fixation. IV) O2 and CO2 diffusion through alveoli.", "options": ["I only", "I, and II", "I, II, and III", "I, II, III, and IV"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q8", "text": "Suppose that scientists determined 75% of polar bear dens were dug on floating sea ice from 1986 to 1994. If this trend were to continue, the percent of polar dens dug on ice on land from 2013 to 2021 would most likely be:", "options": ["Less than 25%", "Between 45% and 65%", "Between 25% and 65%", "Greater than 65%"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q9", "text": "What is true about aerobic respiration and photosynthesis?", "options": ["oxygen is a reactant in aerobic respiration, and CO2 is a product. While in photosynthesis, oxygen is a product and CO2 is a reactant", "oxygen is product in aerobic respiration, while CO2 is reactant. While in photosynthesis, oxygen is reactant and CO2 is product", "no oxygen in photosynthesis, because it produces CO2", "no CO2 in aerobic respiration, because it produces O2"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q10", "text": "There is a plant in normal environment. Then we started to water it by salt water. After one week, what did turgid pressure in plant cells more likely to be lower or higher?", "options": ["turgid pressure will be higher because the plant cell will experience a net gain of water", "turgid pressure will be lower because the plant will experience a net loss of water", "turgid pressure will be higher because the plant will experience a net loss of water", "turgid pressure will be lower because the plant will experience a net gain of water"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q11", "text": "Herbivores can digest cellulose, while other animals cannot. Why?", "options": ["some viruses present in herbivore digestive tract", "some bacteria present in herbivore digestive tract", "herbivore eat cellulose that is already decomposed", "herbivore eat cellulose in small amount"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q12", "text": "What is the type of blood circulation for vertebrates?", "options": ["opened, blood is not confined to heart", "opened, blood enters body cavities without vessels", "closed, blood is confined to heart", "closed, blood enters body cavities with vessels"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q13", "text": "According to Mendel's law of segregation. If 2 heterozygous parents are having a child. What cause probability it will be a homozygous recessive?", "options": ["alleles will get separated during meiosis", "alleles will get separated during mitosis", "alleles will stick to each ot