nfly's larvae prey resulted in decrease the number of bluegills leaving less food for largemouth bass"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q19", "text": "6 groups of plans watered with same amounts of water, germinated with same numbers of seeds under same temperature. But 3 groups placed in dark, and 3 placed in direct light. The groups placed in direct light most likely produce?", "options": ["more CO2 due to respiration", "more CO2 due to photosynthesis", "more O2 due to respiration", "more O2 due to photosynthesis"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q20", "text": "In humans, there is a disease result from a mutation in a single gene. This mutation is an autosomal recessive. The individual with disease must be homozygous or heterozygous for the mutant allele?", "options": ["heterozygous, because diseased individual must have one copy of mutant alle", "heterozygous, because diseased individual must have two copies of mutant alle", "homozygous, because diseased individual must have two copies of mutant alle", "homozygous, because diseased individual must have one copy of mutant alle"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q21", "text": "Which of the following describe the primary function of skin?", "options": ["filter blood", "detoxify blood", "a barrier against infectious agents", "produce bile salt"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q22", "text": "Is a typical male can be heterozygous for a recessive sex-linked disease?", "options": ["no, to be heterozygous, you must have 2 copies of same allele and a male carry only one copy of X chromosome", "no, to be heterozygous, you must have 2 copies of different allele and a male carry only one copy of X chromo