nt-baseline: central; }\n    </style>\n  </defs>\n  <g transform=\"translate(45, 25)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">Patient</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"0\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"235\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">Blood Pressure (mmHg)</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"42\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"63\" class=\"td-text\">Patient A</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"42\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"235\" y=\"63\" class=\"td-val\">140 / 80</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"84\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"105\" class=\"td-text\">Patient B</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"84\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"235\" y=\"105\" class=\"td-val\">130 / 80</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"126\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"147\" class=\"td-text\">Patient C</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"126\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"235\" y=\"147\" class=\"td-val\">120 / 80</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"168\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"189\" class=\"td-text\">Patient D</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"168\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"235\" y=\"189\" class=\"td-val\">100 / 70</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-4-q51", "text": "What of the following choices in not correct?", "options": ["DNA replicate to DNA", "DNA transcript to RNA", "RNA translates to protein", "Protein translates to RNA"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q52", "text": "In an isolated population of sea lions, only 1 allele (allele L) of a particular gene was present. Was this rapid decrease in frequency of allele L more likely the result of gene glow or mutation?", "options": ["Gene flow, a spontaneous change in the DNA that codes for the gene gave rise to a different allele immediately after the new sea lions", "Gene flow, a different allele of the gene was introduced into this population by the new sea lions", "Mutation, a spontaneous change in the DNA that codes for this gene gave rise to a different allele immediately after the new sea lions were introduced", "Mutation, a different allele of the gene was introduced into the population by the new sea lions"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q53", "text": "A scientist is designing an experiment to study how a vitamin affects weight gain in mice. Which of the following procedures should be followed to ensure that any differences in weight gain between the groups will be due to only differences in the vitamin dose?", "options": ["Give the same type and amount of food to each of groups 1-4", "Give different types and amounts of food to each groups 1-4", "Use 1 stain of mice in groups 1-2 and different strains of mice in groups 3-4", "Use female mice in groups 1-2 and male mice in groups 3-4"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q54", "text": "An aqueous 20% sucrose solution was put into a bag. Was the mass more likely greater or less than it was before the bag was added to the distilled H2O?", "options": ["Less, indicating that H2O had exited the bag", "Less, indicating that the sucrose had exited the bag", "Greater, indicating that H2O had entered the bag", "Greater, indicating that sucrose had entered the bag"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 340\" width=\"320\" height=\"340\" style=\"background:#fff; font-fam