m, must be heterozygous for the mutant allele of gene K", "Either man or woman, but not both of them, must be homozygous for mutant allele for gene K", "Both man and woman must be heterozygous for mutant allele for gene K", "Both man and woman must be homozygous for mutant allele for gene 3K"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q57", "text": "Suppose scientists recreate what they are thought the conditions of early earth conditions, by combining hydrogen H2, methane CH4, ammonia NH3, and water H2O in A flask. Then they stimulate lightening by introducing electric sparks. Several days later their analysis of the flask contents would most likely reveal the presence of which of the following?", "options": ["Aerobic heterotrophs", "Amino acids", "Prokaryotes", "Starches"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q58", "text": "Suppose that two groups of warblers population become geographically isolated. Over time the two populations of warblers become different species. Which of the following statements about these two populations is most likely correct?", "options": ["Population A did not evolve", "Population B did not evolve", "There was very little gene flow. If any, between populations A and B", "There was not any genetic divergence between populations A and B"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q59", "text": "What is the sequence of anticodon (shown 3' to 5') of that binds to mRNA codon ACG (shown from 5' to 3')?", "options": ["TGC", "UGC", "CGA", "GUA"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q60", "text": "A codominant pattern of inheritance is one in which:", "options": ["A heterozygote shows the phenotypic effects of one allele for a gene over another allele of same gene", "A heterozygote shous the phenotypic effects of both alleles for a gene equally", "The phenotypic effects of an allele for a gene are observed in a homozygous but not in a heterozygous", "The phenotypic effect of an allele for one gene modifies the phenotypic effects of an allele of a different gene"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q61", "text": "A remora is a fish that attaches to a shark for transportation and consume waste food materials. Assume that an attached remora does not positively or negatively affect the shark, which of the following types of ecological relationships does the example demonstrate?", "options": ["Parasitism", "Neutralism", "Mutualism", "Commensalism"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q62", "text": "For resting human neuron, the concentration of Na outside the neuron is much greater than the concentration of Na inside the neuron. Which of the following processes is responsible for maintaining the Na concentration inside a resting neuron?", "options": ["Simple diffusion", "Facilitated diffusion", "Osmosis", "Active transport"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q63", "text": "In snapdragons, plant height is determined by gene T, flower color is determined by gene R. A student crosses a short red flower with heterozygous tall pink flower. What ratio of plant height and flower colors is predicted from this cross?", "options": ["9 tall red : 3 tall white : 3 short red : 1 short white", "3 tall red : 1 tall pink : 3 short red : 1 short pink", "1 tall red : 1 tall pink : 1 short red : 1 short pink", "1 tall pink : 1 tall white : 1 short pink : 1 short white"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q64", "text": "The stomach contains chyme which is an acidic fluid. The pancreas release bicarbonates(H2CO3) to neutralize the chyme. What happen to chyme when it mixes with bicarbonate?", "options": ["It decreases its acidity by increasing the hydrogen ion concentration", "It decreases its acidity by lowering the hydrogen ion concentration", "It increases its acidity by increasing the hydrogen ion concentration", "It decreases its acidity by increasing the hydrogen ion concentration"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q65", "text": "Which organic compound move from ribosome to rough endoplasmic reticulum to Golgi apparatus?", "options": ["Protein exported outside the cell", "Nucleic acid exported outside the cell", "Protein transported to mitochondria", "Nucleic acid transported to mitochondria"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q66", "text": "A scientist measures the number of organisms to collect data: amoeba 15, paramecium 9, algae 18, volvox 8. What is the percentage of amoeba?", "options": ["50%", "30%", "15%", "18%"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 270\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"background:#ffffff; font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\">\n  <defs>\n    <style>\n      .th-bg { fill: #f8fafc; stroke: #cbd5e1; stroke-width: 1.5; }\n      .td-bg-even { fill: #ffffff; stroke: #e2e8f0; stroke-width: 1; }\n      .td-bg-odd { fill: #f8fafc; stroke: #e2e8f0; stroke-width: 1; }\n      .th-text { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: #0f172a; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n      .td-organism { font-size: 13.5px; font-style: italic; font-weight: 600; fill: #1e293b; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n   