ent B suggest that partly energy is lost through animal faeces", "both students have correct conclusions", "neither student have correct conclusions"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q68", "text": "Which subatomic particles have an electrical reaction between them?", "options": ["Neutrons and protons", "Electrons and protons", "Electrons and neutrons", "All subatomic particles"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q69", "text": "Scientists used many observations to determine the structure of the DNA molecule. Which of the following observations provided the strong evidence that guanine form hydrogen bonds with cytosine, as opposed to forming hydrogen bonds with adenine or thymine?", "options": ["The same carbon-based ring structure is present in both guanine and cytosine", "The percentage of guanine bases equals the percentage of cytosine", "The same type of sugar molecule attaches to guanine as attaches to cytosine", "The number of deoxyribose molecules equals the number of guanine and cytosine bases combined"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q70", "text": "Which of the following meiotic events provides support for Mendel's law of segregation?", "options": ["Homologous chromosomes separate from one another during anaphase I", "Homologous chromosomes exchange segments of DNA during anaphase I", "Sister chromatids separate from one another during anaphase II", "Sister chromatids exchange segments of DNA during anaphase II"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q71", "text": "Which of the following listed are true about viruses? I. They can not reproduce without a host. II. They are not made up of 1 or more cells. III. They don't contain genetic material.", "options": ["III only", "I and II only", "II and III only", "I, III, and III only"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q72", "text": "The nutritional composition of each of 3 different cereals is shown in the table. What is the order of the cereals from greatest to the least amount of energy per 90g serving?", "options": ["Cereal 1 > cereal 2 > cereal 3", "Cereal 1 > cereal 3 > cereal 2", "Cereal 2 > cereal 1 > cereal 3", "Cereal 2 > cereal 3 > cereal 1"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 230\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"background:#ffffff; font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\">\n  <defs>\n    <style>\n      .th-bg { fill: #f8fafc; stroke: #cbd5e1; stroke-width: 1.5; }\n      .td-bg-even { fill: #ffffff; stroke: #e2e8f0; stroke-width: 1; }\n      .td-bg-odd { fill: #f8fafc; stroke: #e2e8f0; stroke-width: 1; }\n      .th-text { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: #0f172a; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n      .td-text { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 600; fill: #334155; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n      .td-val { font-size: 13.5px; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, Menlo, monospace; font-weight: 700; fill: #1e293b; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n    </style>\n  </defs>\n  <g transform=\"translate(40, 25)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">Cereal</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"0\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">Fat (g)</text>\n    <rect x=\"260\" y=\"0\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">Protein (g)</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"42\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"63\" class=\"td-text\">Cereal 1</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"42\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"63\" class=\"td-val\">10 g</text>\n    <rect x=\"260\" y=\"42\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"63\" class=\"td-val\">40 g</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"84\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"105\" class=\"td-text\">Cereal 2</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"84\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"105\" class=\"td-val\">40 g</text>\n    <rect x=\"260\" y=\"84\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"105\" class=\"td-val\">30 g</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"126\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"70\" y=\"147\" class=\"td-text\">Cereal 3</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"126\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"147\" class=\"td-val\">30 g</text>\n    <rect x=\"260\" y=\"126\" width=\"120\" height=\"42\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"147\" class=\"td-val\">30 g</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-4-q73", "text": "The molecule that is the building block of cell membrane?", "options": ["Protein", "Lipid", "Carbohydrate", "Nucleic acid"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q74", "text": "Which of the following best describe an enzyme?", "options": ["A catalyst that speeds up a specific biochemical reaction", "A substance that slows down a specific biochemical reaction", "A catalyst that is consumed in a biochemical reaction", "A substance that is not consumed in a biochemical reaction"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q75", "text": "Aerobic respiration yields more ATP molecules per glucose molecule that does anaerobic respiration. Which 2 cellular processes are responsible for larger ATP yield during aerobic respiration?", "options": ["Glycolysis and fermentation", "Glycolysis and Krebs cycle", "Electron transport chain and fermentation", "Electron transport chain and Krebs cycle"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q76", "text": "Suppose a parent cell undergoes mitotic division resulting in formation of 2 daughter cells. Compared to the number of chromosomes in a parent cell, the number of chromosomes in daughter cell will be typically:", "options": ["1/4 as greater", "1/2 as greater", "3 times as greater", "The same"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q77", "text": "Which type of cell is most directly affected by sickle-cell anaemia?", "options": ["Nerve cell", "Red blood cell", "White blood cell", "Smooth muscle cell"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q78", "text": "This diagram represents partial cladogram of vertebrates: Which of the following statements most accurately describes the phenotypic similarities between lungfish and another group of organisms in this cladogram?", "options": ["Lungfish and sharks both have vertebrae, but share no other characteristics", "Lungfish and lampreys both have vertebrae, but only lungfish have jaws", "Lungfish and ray-finned fish both have bony ribs, but only lungfish have jaws", "Lungfish and amphibians both have bony ribs, but share no other characteristics"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 360\" width=\"600\" height=\"360\" style=\"background:#fff; font-family:sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\">Vertebrate Trait Cladogram</text>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"296\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Lampreys</text>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sharks</text>\n  <line x1=\"260\" y1=\"212\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ray-finned fish</text>\n  <line x1=\"330\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"305\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0284c7\">Lungfish</text>\n  <line x1=\"410\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"390\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Amphibians</text>\n  <line x1=\"480\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"475\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"475\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Land vertebrates</text>\n  <g font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">\n    <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"308\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"308\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"170\" y=\"312\">Vertebrae</text>\n    <line x1=\"150\" y1=\"278\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"278\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"220\" y=\"282\">Jaws</text>\n    <line x1=\"220\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"240\">Bony ribs &amp; shoulder girdle</text>\n    <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"188\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"390\" y=\"192\">Choanae</text>\n    <line x1=\"375\" y1=\"143\" x2=\"455\" y2=\"143\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"465\" y=\"147\">Fingers and toes</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-4-q79", "text": "Students in a biology class measured the body lengths of 5 fruit flies. The students determined that the average body length of the 5 flies was 0.8 mm. Which of the following data sets represents the possible body lengths of the 5 fruit flies?", "options": ["0.5 mm, 0.5 mm, 0.6 mm, 0.7 mm, 0.8 mm", "0.6 mm, 0.7 mm, 0.8 mm, 0.9 mm, 1.0 mm", "0.7 mm, 0.8 mm, 0.9 mm, 0.9 mm, 1.5 mm", "0.8 mm, 0.9 mm, 1.2 mm, 1.4 mm, 1.8 mm"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q80", "text": "Sierra sulphur butterflies live in high-altitude meadows of California Sierra Nevada. Which of the following terms best describes an interbreeding group of Sierra sulphur butterflies?", "options": ["Biome", "Community", "Ecosystem", "Population"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q81", "text": "A student that the red blood cells swell when added to test tube filled with distilled water, and eventually burst. Which of the following statement best explain why cell burst? The water concentration was higher:", "options": ["Inside the cell than outside, so more water diffused out of the cell than into the cell", "outside the cell than inside, so more water diffused out of the cell than into the cell", "inside the cell than outside, so more water diffused into the cell than out of the cell", "Outside the cell than inside, so more water diffused into of the cell than out of the cell"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q82", "text": "A scientist calculates the amount of oxygen produced by plant through time intervals. What is the average rate of 3 mins?", "options": ["9.1 Liter/min", "14.8 Liter/min", "22.3 Liter/min", "27.3 Liter/min"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 380\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" style=\"background:#ffffff; font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\">\n  <defs>\n    <style>\n      .th-bg { fill: #f8fafc; stroke: #cbd5e1; stroke-width: 1.5; }\n      .td-bg-even { fill: #ffffff; stroke: #e2e8f0; stroke-width: 1; }\n      .td-bg-odd { fill: #f8fafc; stroke: #e2e8f0; stroke-width: 1; }\n      .th-text { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: #0f172a; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n      .td-val { font-size: 13.5px; font-family: 'SF Mono', Consolas, Menlo, monospace; font-weight: 600; fill: #1e293b; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: central; }\n    </style>\n  </defs>\n  <g transform=\"translate(50, 20)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"170\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">Time (sec)</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"0\" width=\"190\" height=\"42\" class=\"th-bg\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"21\" class=\"th-text\">O₂ Production (Liter)</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"42\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"62\" class=\"td-val\">0</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"42\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"62\" class=\"td-val\">0</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"82\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"102\" class=\"td-val\">30</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"82\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"102\" class=\"td-val\">7.0</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"122\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"142\" class=\"td-val\">60</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"122\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"142\" class=\"td-val\">12.5</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"162\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"182\" class=\"td-val\">90</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"162\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"182\" class=\"td-val\">17.8</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"202\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"222\" class=\"td-val\">120</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"202\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"222\" class=\"td-val\">22.4</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"242\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"262\" class=\"td-val\">150</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"242\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-odd\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"262\" class=\"td-val\">25.2</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"282\" width=\"170\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"85\" y=\"302\" class=\"td-val\">180</text>\n    <rect x=\"170\" y=\"282\" width=\"190\" height=\"40\" class=\"td-bg-even\"/>\n    <text x=\"265\" y=\"302\" class=\"td-val\">27.3</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-4-q83", "text": "Suppose in rabbits, a particular point mutation in gene F results in long whiskers phenotype that has an autosomal dominant mode of inheritance. If 2 rabbits that are heterozygous for long whiskers allele produce offspring, what is the percent chance that the offspring will have long whiskers?", "options": ["25%", "50%", "75%", "100%"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q84", "text": "Which of the following is the most likely reason why many enzymes in human body do not function at temperature significantly higher than normal body temperature? At higher temperature, the", "options": ["Enzyme begins to denature preventing the substrate from binding to the active site of the enzyme", "Substrate begins to denature, preventing the enzyme from binding to the active site of the substrate", "Enzyme may become different chemical substrate, enabling the enzyme to bind with other substrates in the body", "Substrate may become different chemical substrate, enabling the substrate to bind with other enzymes in the body"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q85", "text": "When sea otter was removed from this food chain, the population of sea urchins increased dramatically. The removal of sea otters from food chain could have contributed to the increase in population of sea urchins by:", "options": ["Decreasing competition between sea otters and sea urchins for kelp", "Increasing competition between sea otters and sea urchins for kelp", "Decreasing predation pressure by sea otters, allowing more sea urchins to survive longer to produce more offspring", "Increasing predation pressure by sea otters, preventing most of the sea urchins from surviving to produce offspring"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 300\" width=\"420\" height=\"300\" style=\"background:#e0f2fe; font-family:sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0369a1\">Simple Marine Food Chain</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60, 210)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#15803d\"/>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Giant Kelp</text>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#166534\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Producer)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(60, 60)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#9333ea\"/>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sea Urchin</text>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"-10\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7e22ce\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Primary Consumer)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(260, 60)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c2410c\"/>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sea Otter</text>\n    <text x=\"55\" y=\"-10\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#9a3412\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Secondary Consumer)</text>\n  </g>\n  <line x1=\"115\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"115\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"115,105 110,118 120,118\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/>\n  <line x1=\"170\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"260,82 247,77 247,87\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-4-q86", "text": "Which of the following statements comparing viruses to bacteria is typically correct? Unlike most bacteria, viruses:", "options": ["Require a living host to multiply", "Are single celled organism", "Are killed by antibiotic", "Produce their food by photosynthesis"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q87", "text": "If a woman has 1 dominant allele and 1 recessive allele of a gene located on the X chromosome, and a man has a dominant allele of this gene, produce a son. Is the percent chance that their son will have the recessive phenotype 0% or 50%?", "options": ["0%, because the son will inherit a dominant allele frm his father", "0%, because the son will inherit a dominant allele from their mother", "50%, because the probability that the son will inherit a Y chromosome from his father is 50%", "50%, because the probability that the son will inherit the recessive allele from his mother is 50%"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-4-q88", "text": "Which of the following is a characteristic of all dogs, trees, and mushrooms? They all are:", "options": ["Producers", "Consumers", "Prokaryotes", "Eukaryotes"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 4", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}]}, {"id": "act-5", "title": "ACT — Test 5", "meta": "79 questions · Biology section", "questions": [{"id": "act-5-q1", "text": "Suppose a female bat has a total of 44 chromosomes in each of its diploid cells. How many individual chromosomes will most likely be in each of its gametes?", "options": ["88 chromosomes", "22 chromosomes", "11 chromosomes", "44 chromosomes"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q2", "text": "Which of the following is a characteristic of all organic molecules?", "options": ["They are made up of ionic bonds", "They undergo hydrogen bonding", "They are insoluble in water", "They contain carbon atoms"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q3", "text": "By which process do cells use energy to move substances across a membrane?", "options": ["Active transport", "Diffusion", "Osmosis", "Passive Transport"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q4", "text": "Which of the following statements is the most complete and accurate description of meiosis?", "options": ["A single division of a haploid cell produces haploid gametes", "A single division of a diploid cell produces diploid gametes", "Two successive cell divisions produce haploid gametes", "Two successive cell divisions produce diploid gametes"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q5", "text": "Max wants to determine the effects of plant hormone auxin on root growth. He places 10 plant cuttings into each of 4 different aqueous solutions: 0% auxin, 0.02% auxin, 0.2% auxin, and 2.0% auxin. Which of these solutions is the control for this experiment?", "options": ["0% auxin", "0.2% auxin", "0.02% auxin", "2.0% auxin"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q6", "text": "In 1956, Arthur Kornberg isolated DNA polymerase, an enzyme that replicates DNA. In which of the following eukaryotic cellular components is DNA polymerase typically active?", "options": ["Centriole", "Nucleus", "Lysosome", "Ribosome"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q7", "text": "To determine the mean number of plant species per sampling plot, an ecologist counts the number of plant species in 10 different plots. She finds the following: Three plots have 7 plant species each; Two plots have 6 plant species each; Three plots have 5 plant species each; Two plots have 4 plant species each. What is the mean number of plant species per sampling plot?", "options": ["6.0", "5.6", "5.2", "4.8"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q8", "text": "In humans, individuals with codominant alleles for a given gene express how many alleles of that gene?", "options": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q9", "text": "Which of the following is a common function of lipids?", "options": ["Building cellulose within cell walls", "Catalyzing chemical reactions in the cell", "Encoding genetic information in living organisms", "Forming a boundary as part of the plasma membrane"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q10", "text": "On a microscope slide containing animal tissue, Sarah observes many long, thin cells lying parallel to each other within tight bundles. Stripes, or striations, appear perpendicular to the lengths of these cells. Which tissue type is Sarah most likely observing?", "options": ["Muscle", "Connective", "Epithelial", "Nervous"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q11", "text": "One reason that the light-independent reactions of photosynthesis do NOT continue to occur throughout periods of prolonged darkness is because the light-independent reactions:", "options": ["Require CO2 produced by the light-dependent reactions", "Require ATP and NADPH produced by the light-dependent reactions", "Produce CO2 required by the light-dependent reactions", "Produce ATP and NADPH required by the light-dependent reactions"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q12", "text": "In 1958, Meselson and Stahl determined that the process of DNA replication is semi-conservative. In DNA molecules produced by semi-conservative DNA replication, each double helix contains:", "options": ["2 new strands of DNA", "2 parental strands of DNA", "1 new strand of DNA and 1 new strand of RNA", "1 new strand of DNA and 1 parental strand of DNA"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q13", "text": "A student places a basket of peaches in a dark kitchen cabinet. One week later the student observes mold growing on the peaches. The student purchases 10 peaches, places 5 in a dark compartment of a refrigerator, and places the remaining 5 peaches in a dark cabinet. One week later the student examines both sets of peaches for mold growth. Which of the following questions about mold was the student most likely trying to answer?", "options": ["Does mold grow in the dark?", "Does mold grow at room temperature?", "Does mold grow faster in dark or in light?", "Does mold grow faster at room temperature or at cooler temperature?"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q14", "text": "When grown under ideal conditions, Escherichia coli bacteria populations double every 20 minutes. A student inoculates culture medium with 100 E. coli cells and grows them under ideal conditions. How many times must these cells double in number for this bacterial population to surpass 3,000 cells?", "options": ["3", "7", "5", "9"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q15", "text": "Which of the following statements correctly identifies the charge of a subatomic particle and best describes the location of that particle in the atom?", "options": ["An electron is positive, and it is located outside the nucleus", "An electron is negative, and it is located inside the nucleus", "A proton has no charge, and it is located outside the nucleus", "A neutron has no charge, and it is located inside the nucleus"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q16", "text": "A biology student observed prepared microscope slides and recorded these observations in her lab notes: Centromeres split; Sister chromatids pulled apart to opposite poles. What phase of mitosis is described in her notes?", "options": ["Anaphase", "Metaphase", "Prophase", "Telophase"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q17", "text": "Activation of motor neurons allows humans to move parts of the body. This activation occurs when a chemical messenger moves into the space between the plasma membrane of a neuron and the plasma membrane of a muscle cell. The space between these plasma membranes is part of the:", "options": ["Terminal axon", "Synapse", "Neurotransmitter", "Vesicle"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q18", "text": "A student observed that when red blood cells were added to a test tube containing distilled water, the cells swelled and eventually burst. Which of the following statements best explains why the cells burst? The salt concentration was higher:", "options": ["Inside the cells than outside the cells, so more water diffused out of the cells than into the cells", "Outside the cells than inside the cells, so more water diffused out of the cells than into the cells", "Inside the cells than outside the cells, so more water diffused into the cells than out of the cells", "Outside the cells than inside the cells, so more water diffused into the cells than out of the cells"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q19", "text": "In pea plants, round pea shape is a dominant trait and wrinkled pea is a recessive trait. When a pea plant grown from a round pea is crossed with a pea plant grown from a wrinkled pea, the resulting offspring are 52 round peas and 65 wrinkled peas. Which of the following best describes the genotype of the parent grown from the round pea?", "options": ["Heterozygous", "Codominant", "Homozygous dominant", "Homozygous recessive"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q20", "text": "Within the system of binomial nomenclature, what do Quercus rubra & Quercus alba represent?", "options": ["2 genera that are members of the same family", "2 genera that are members of the same species", "2 species that are members of the same genus", "2 subspecies that are members of the same species"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q21", "text": "Specialized cells of the pancreas produce insulin. Which of the following observations most strongly supports the conclusion that it is the IDX-1 gene that regulates insulin production?", "options": ["The IDX-1 gene is present in all body cells, including the pancreas", "The IDX-1 gene is present in both liver and pancreas cells but is expressed only in liver cells", "Products of the IDX-1 gene bind to DNA, regulating insulin gene transcription", "Mutations of the IDX gene have no effect on the regulation of insulin production"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q22", "text": "Many molecules are necessary for transcription and for translation. Which of the following types of molecules is directly involved in transcription, but is NOT directly involved in translation?", "options": ["DNA", "Protein", "mRNA", "tRNA"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q23", "text": "A certain plant stores toxic chemicals that, if ingested, are harmful to some animals. This toxic chemical is most likely stored in which of the following types of organelles?", "options": ["Vacuole", "Mitochondrion", "Ribosome", "Chloroplast"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q24", "text": "A shark feeding on a fish, a fox feeding on a rabbit, and a bird feeding on an insect are all examples of which of the following types of interaction?", "options": ["Competition", "Mutualism", "Herbivory", "Predation"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q25", "text": "In vascular plants, which of the following best describes the component of the vascular system that transports sugars and organic nutrients throughout the plant?", "options": ["Cuticle", "Phloem", "Cortex", "Xylem"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q26", "text": "Which of the following choices describes a primary function of skin?", "options": ["Serving as a barrier against infectious organisms", "Preventing the elimination of waste from the body", "Preventing the regulation of body temperature", "Allowing ultraviolet radiation to affect deep tissues"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q27", "text": "Which of the following statements best describes how organic compounds differ from inorganic compounds?", "options": ["Organic compounds always contain both carbon and hydrogen", "Organic compounds always contain ionic bonds", "Inorganic compounds always contain both carbon and hydrogen", "Inorganic compounds always contain covalent bonds"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q28", "text": "Seven species of Anolis lizards successfully coexist in the same habitat and feed on insects and other arthropods. Which of the following statements best explains their ability to coexist in the same habitat?", "options": ["The species have different reproductive cycles", "Individuals fail to identify others as belonging to different species", "High levels of competition exist between members of the 7 species", "Each species occupies a distinct niche"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q29", "text": "Which of the following statements best describes gene expression in a multicellular organism? Each cell has:", "options": ["The same set of genes and all the genes are expressed in each cell type", "The same set of genes, but has only certain genes that are expressed in each cell type", "A different set of genes and all those genes are expressed in each cell type", "A different set of genes has only certain genes that are expressed in each cell type"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q30", "text": "A peptide bond is formed between molecules of which type?", "options": ["Amino acids", "Monosaccharides", "Fatty acids", "Nucleotides"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q31", "text": "Electron microscope analysis revealed extensive damage to the Golgi apparatus within a liver cell. Damage to the Golgi apparatus will most likely have which of the following cellular consequences?", "options": ["Protein products will be modified for use inside the damaged cells", "Protein products will not be secreted from the damaged cells", "Translation will not occur within cytoplasmic vesicles in the damaged cells", "Transcription will be limited to cytoplasmic vesicles of the damaged cells"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q32", "text": "Cilia are present on Paramecium caudatum. Flagella are present on Giardia lamblia. Compared to the flagella of G. lamblia, the cilia of P. caudatum are typically:", "options": ["Shorter and fewer in number", "Longer and fewer in number", "Shorter and greater in number", "Longer and greater in number"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q33", "text": "Which of these is a difference between bacteria and protists?", "options": ["Bacteria consist of cells but protists do not", "Bacteria have RNA but protists have DNA", "Bacteria use photosynthesis but protists do not", "Bacteria do not have a nucleus, but protists do"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q34", "text": "A student designed an experiment to determine the effect of using a lattice on plant growth. For 3 weeks, the student grew 10 plants: 5 using a lattice and 5 without using a lattice. The student then measured the height of each plant. What was the dependent variable in the student's experiment?", "options": ["Number of plants with a lattice", "Length of time plants grew", "Presence or absence of a lattice", "Height of plant"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q35", "text": "Molecule X and molecule Y have slightly different shapes. An enzyme reacts with molecule X, but it does not react with molecule Y. Based on this information, which of the following statements best explains this difference in the reactivity of the enzyme with these 2 molecules?", "options": ["Molecule X has less energy, making it more attractive for the enzyme", "Molecule X transfers protons that allow the enzyme to work", "Molecule Y does not require the enzyme to break down", "Molecule Y does not fit properly into the active site of the enzyme"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q36", "text": "While on the HMS Beagle, Charles Darwin made a stop at the Galapagos Islands. He observed that on islands with tortoise populations, prickly pear cactus fruits grew far above the ground. On islands without tortoise populations, prickly pear cactus fruits grew on or near the ground. These observations led Darwin to conclude that the tortoises acted as agents of selection on the prickly pear cacti by feeding on:", "options": ["Fruits from other species in the area", "Prickly pear cactus fruits growing anywhere on the cacti", "Prickly pear cactus fruits growing high above the ground only", "Prickly pear cactus fruits growing on or near the ground only"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q37", "text": "Fossils of the land-dwelling mammal-like reptile Lystrosaurus (millions of years old) have been found in Africa, India, Madagascar, and Antarctica. This map shows these locations on Earth. Which of the following statements provides the most likely explanation for the existence of Lystrosaurus in all 4 areas?", "options": ["Lystrosaurus bones drifted through the oceans and fossilized when they landed in continental sedimentary rocks", "Lystrosaurus swam between continents and survived the extreme temperature of Antarctica", "Lystrosaurus evolved on each continent independently and then went extinct", "Lystrosaurus lived and walked on these lands when they were once connected as one land mass"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 650 340\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"650\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"325\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"300\" ry=\"150\" fill=\"#e0f2fe\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M120,60 Q180,50 210,90 Q220,130 190,145 Q160,140 140,110 Z\" fill=\"#22c55e\" stroke=\"#15803d\"/>\n  <path d=\"M185,155 Q230,175 220,230 Q200,270 175,250 Q165,190 185,155 Z\" fill=\"#16a34a\" stroke=\"#15803d\"/>\n  <path d=\"M300,70 Q450,50 540,90 Q550,150 480,165 Q420,130 360,130 Q310,100 300,70 Z\" fill=\"#ea580c\" stroke=\"#c2410c\"/>\n  <path d=\"M290,120 Q365,120 375,170 Q370,225 330,245 Q295,200 290,120 Z\" fill=\"#eab308\" stroke=\"#ca8a04\"/>\n  <path d=\"M480,200 Q540,195 545,230 Q515,250 475,235 Z\" fill=\"#db2777\" stroke=\"#be185d\"/>\n  <path d=\"M160,290 Q325,270 490,290 Q400,315 250,315 Z\" fill=\"#2563eb\" stroke=\"#1d4ed8\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"335\" cy=\"205\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#dc2626\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"345\" y=\"210\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#7f1d1d\">Africa</text>\n  <circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"215\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#dc2626\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"390\" y=\"220\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#7f1d1d\">Madagascar</text>\n  <circle cx=\"430\" cy=\"155\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#dc2626\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\