\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\">G</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"240\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\">GCU, GCC, GCA, GCG -&gt; Ala (Alanine)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q47", "text": "If individual 9 and an affected male with Dubin-Johnson syndrome plan to have a child, what is the percentage chance that the child will inherit Dubin-Johnson syndrome?", "options": ["0%", "50%", "25%", "100%"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect x=\"175\" y=\"30\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"188\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">1</text>\n  <line x1=\"201\" y1=\"43\" x2=\"245\" y2=\"43\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"258\" cy=\"43\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n  <text x=\"258\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">2</text>\n  <line x1=\"223\" y1=\"43\" x2=\"223\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"123\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">4</text>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"110\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n  <text x=\"53\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">3</text>\n  <line x1=\"66\" y1=\"123\" x2=\"87\" y2=\"123\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"175\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"162\" y=\"110\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"175\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">5</text>\n  <line x1=\"245\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"245\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"123\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"245\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">6</text>\n  <line x1=\"320\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"123\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">7</text>\n  <line x1=\"333\" y1=\"123\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"123\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"370\" y=\"110\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"383\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">8</text>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"123\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"208\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">9</text>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"208\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">10</text>\n  <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"97\" y=\"195\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n  <text x=\"110\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">11</text>\n  <line x1=\"150\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"208\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\">12</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(430, 30)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"24\" y=\"13\" font-size=\"10\">Unaffected male</text>\n    <circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"35\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"24\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"10\">Unaffected female</text>\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"55\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n    <text x=\"24\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"10\">Affected male</text>\n    <circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"90\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#000\"/>\n    <text x=\"24\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10\">Affected female</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q48", "text": "Student 1 argues that plants produce sugars through photosynthesis and do not carry out cellular respiration. Student 2 insists that plants must carry out both photosynthesis and cellular respiration to survive. Who is correct, and why?", "options": ["Student 1, because plants both store and release all the energy they need during photosynthesis", "Student 1, because plants acquire solar energy using chlorophyll, but animals use cellular respiration to generate usable energy", "Student 2, because plants store and release some energy during photosynthesis and store energy during cellular respiration", "Student 2, because plants store energy during photosynthesis and they use cellular respiration to release energy for life functions"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q49", "text": "A scientist observes a segmented organism with long fangs (chelicerae), a chitinous exoskeleton, and 8 jointed walking appendages. Based on these characteristics, the organism most likely belongs to which of the following phyla?", "options": ["Arthropoda", "Echinodermata", "Chordata", "Mollusca"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q50", "text": "Which of the following statements best describes a way that the misuse of antibiotics contributes to the spread of resistant strains of bacteria? The misuse of antibiotics can result in:", "options": ["A decrease in the frequency of antibiotic resistance genes in a population of bacteria", "An increase in the frequency of antibiotic resistance genes in a population of bacteria", "The transfer of nuclei from bacteria to viruses", "The transfer of nuclei from viruses to bacteria"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q51", "text": "Two genes will most likely assort independently of each other if they are located on:", "options": ["An X chromosome", "A dominant chromosome", "A Y chromosome", "Non-homologous chromosomes"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q52", "text": "Tiny single-celled algae called zooxanthellae live inside the bodies of reef-building corals. Through photosynthesis, zooxanthellae provide corals with carbohydrates, oxygen, and the proper pH to build coral skeletons. The corals provide the zooxanthellae with a safe environment, a source of carbon dioxide, and nutrients. What type of interaction is this?", "options": ["Commensalism", "Mutualism", "Competition", "Parasitism"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q53", "text": "Students were asked to use a microscope to determine whether the cells on a slide were plant cells or cyanobacteria. Based on their observations, the students determined that the slides contained plant cells because plant cells:", "options": ["Have ribosomes and cyanobacteria cells do not", "Have a nucleus and cyanobacteria cells do not", "Do not have lysosomes and cyanobacteria cells do", "Do not have centrioles and cyanobacteria cells do"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q54", "text": "A group of students wants to compare the respiration rate of salmon at 15°C to the respiration rate of salmon at 25°C. A valid comparison could be achieved by determining the average respiration rate of a group of:", "options": ["10 salmon in freshwater at 15°C and a group of 10 salmon in freshwater at 25°C", "10 salmon in freshwater at 15°C and a group of 10 salmon in salt water at 25°C", "10 trout in freshwater at 15°C and a group of 10 salmon in freshwater at 25°C", "10 trout in freshwater at 15°C and a group of 10 salmon in salt water at 25°C"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q55", "text": "Which of the following is a valid unit of measure for the mass of an organism?", "options": ["Meters", "Grams", "Degrees", "Liters"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q56", "text": "The pigment carotene is responsible for the orange color of carrots and many other fruits and vegetables. Which of the following statements best explains why plants that contain carotene appear orange?", "options": ["Carotene strongly absorbs both blue-green light and yellow-orange light", "Carotene strongly absorbs blue-green light, but does not strongly absorb yellow-orange light", "Carotene does not strongly absorb blue-green light, but strongly absorbs yellow-orange light", "Carotene strongly absorbs neither blue-green light nor yellow-orange light"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q57", "text": "Destruction of habitat may cause continuous populations to be fragmented into smaller ones. Genetic diversity within each of these smaller populations may decline over time. Significant loss of genetic diversity will most likely have which of the following effects on a population?", "options": ["Decrease the population's ability to adapt to future environmental challenges", "Increase the population's likelihood of increased predation", "Decrease the population's likelihood of going extinct", "Increase the population's ability to resist diseases"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q58", "text": "The attraction between water molecules is an example of which of the following?", "options": ["Adhesion", "Evaporation", "Cohesion", "Transpiration"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q59", "text": "Which of the following is the best definition of biological evolution?", "options": ["The spontaneous appearance of life from nonliving matter after the formation of Earth", "The series of developmental changes an organism experiences through the course of its lifetime", "A change in the proportions of inherited traits within a population occurring over successive generations", "A means by which random chance blends the characteristics an organism inherits from its parents following fertilization"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q60", "text": "Which of the following is a characteristic of all organic molecules?", "options": ["They are made up of ionic bonds", "They undergo hydrogen bonding", "They are insoluble in water", "They contain carbon atoms"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q61", "text": "How do carbohydrates normally function within the human body?", "options": ["As an energy source", "As enzymes regulating metabolic processes", "As the functional units of fats", "As the primary components of cell membranes"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q62", "text": "Which of the following chemical equations represents a summary of cellular respiration?", "options": ["C6H12O6 + 6O2 -> 6CO2 + 6H2O + ATP", "C6H12O6 -> 2C2H5OH + 2CO2 + ATP", "2C2H4O2 + CO2 + light energy -> C6H12O6 + O2", "6CO2 + 6H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 + 6O2"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q63", "text": "A region in Australia has an average annual temperature of 25°C and an average annual precipitation of 385 cm. According to this diagram, which type of biome is most likely found in this region?", "options": ["Temperate deciduous forest", "Tropical rain forest", "Temperate rain forest", "Tropical seasonal forest"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 380\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"520\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#0f172a\" rx=\"6\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"480\" y2=\"320\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">Average Annual Temperature (°C)</text>\n  <text x=\"25\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 25 180)\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">Annual Precipitation (cm)</text>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">-10</text>\n  <text x=\"172\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">0</text>\n  <text x=\"275\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">10</text>\n  <text x=\"377\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">20</text>\n  <text x=\"480\" y=\"338\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">30</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">0</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">100</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">200</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">300</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\">400</text>\n  <polygon points=\"380,180 430,40 480,140 480,240 380,220\" fill=\"#15803d\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"440\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tropical Rainforest</text>\n  <polygon points=\"275,220 380,180 380,250 275,270\" fill=\"#0284c7\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"10\">Temperate Rainforest</text>\n  <circle cx=\"430\" cy=\"50\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#ef4444\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"415\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fca5a5\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">(25°C, 385 cm)</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q64", "text": "Suppose a cell in prophase I of meiosis contains 12 picograms (pg) of DNA. At the completion of meiosis, the mass of DNA in each gamete will most likely be closest to which of the following masses?", "options": ["3 pg", "12 pg", "6 pg", "24 pg"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q65", "text": "Gabriel finds the concentration of glucose in his blood is approximately 10 times greater than the concentration of glucose in certain cells in his body. The process by which glucose is transported to these cells from his bloodstream is best described by which of the following?", "options": ["Active transport", "Osmosis", "Facilitated diffusion", "Glycolysis"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q66", "text": "Many orchids live in tropical rain forests high in tree branches. They receive water and nutrients that fall from trees' upper leaves. However, their roots don't connect to the trees and they provide no benefit to the trees. What kind of ecological interaction is this?", "options": ["Commensalism", "Mutualism", "Competition", "Parasitism"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q67", "text": "Dr. Garcia collected this data as she studied the relationship between average annual rainfall and the size of mosquito populations. Use the data in the graph to determine which relationship, if any, exists between the average annual rainfall and the number of mosquitoes.", "options": ["There is no relationship", "There is a negative linear relationship", "There is an exponential relationship", "There is a positive linear relationship"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 450 320\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"450\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n  <text x=\"240\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mosquito Population vs. Rainfall</text>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"70\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"235\" y=\"295\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rainfall</text>\n  <text x=\"25\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 25 155)\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mosquito Population</text>\n  <g fill=\"#0f172a\">\n    <circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"235\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"205\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"215\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"215\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"180\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"155\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"170\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"205\" cy=\"190\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"158\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"145\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"165\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"130\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"255\" cy=\"150\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"265\" cy=\"115\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"275\" cy=\"130\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"98\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"110\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"85\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"78\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"345\" cy=\"70\" r=\"4.5\"/>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q68", "text": "The food source for a population of black-bellied seedcrackers consists of seeds that tend to have either large or small sizes. Very few seedcrackers have medium-sized beaks. Hard seeds can be readily eaten only by birds with large beaks; soft seeds can be readily eaten only by birds with small beaks. Based on this information, is the population of seedcrackers more likely influenced by directional selection or by disruptive selection?", "options": ["Directional; this type of selection favors the intermediate form of a trait", "Directional; this type of selection favors the 2 extreme forms of a trait", "Disruptive; this type of selection favors the intermediate form of a trait", "Disruptive; this type of selection favors the 2 extreme forms of a trait"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q69", "text": "What cell type functions to eliminate infection in the human body?", "options": ["Muscle cells", "Skin cells", "Red blood cells", "White blood cells"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q70", "text": "Which statement describes a fundamental characteristic of all living organisms?", "options": ["Inheritance of traits is based on a universal genetic code", "Genetic mutations arise in response to environmental changes", "Cells are interchangeable", "Individual organisms can be identified by microscopic cellular examination"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q71", "text": "Which of the following best describes an ecological community?", "options": ["A group of populations of different species that occupy the same geographical region", "A group of populations of different species and their abiotic environment", "A group of organisms of the same species living in the same geographical environment", "A particular place in which a specific species lives"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q72", "text": "In the 1920s, biochemist Phoebus Levene proposed that DNA contains equal amounts of each nitrogen base and that bases are organized in repeating clusters of 4. Which of the following statements best reflects Chargaff's 1947 correction of Levene's proposed DNA structure?", "options": ["DNA contains unequal amounts of adenine, cytosine, guanine, and thymine", "DNA contains equal amounts of adenine and guanine and unequal amounts of cytosine and thymine", "DNA contains equal amounts of adenine and cytosine and equal amounts of guanine and thymine", "DNA contains equal amounts of adenine and thymine and equal amounts of cytosine and guanine"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q73", "text": "A form of vitamin D-resistant rickets is inherited as an X-linked dominant disease. Suppose a man with this disease and a woman without this disease produce 2 children: 1 male and 1 female. Which of these children would be likely to inherit the allele for vitamin D-resistant rickets?", "options": ["Neither child", "The male only", "Both children", "The female only"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q74", "text": "In living cells, Enzyme X facilitates a reaction that breaks down hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen. Which of the following statements about Enzyme X is most likely correct?", "options": ["Enzyme X lowers the activation energy of the reaction", "Enzyme X is consumed during the reaction", "Enzyme X is permanently altered during the reaction", "Enzyme X is unaffected by extreme changes in temperature and pH"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q75", "text": "Which of the following statements accurately compares rain to another substance in the table?", "options": ["Rain has a higher hydroxide ion concentration than ammonia", "Rain has a higher hydroxide ion concentration than milk", "Rain has a lower hydroxide ion concentration than vinegar", "Rain has a lower hydroxide ion concentration than lye"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 310\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"420\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" rx=\"6\"/>\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"25\" width=\"360\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"230\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"285\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"83\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"83\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"111\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"111\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"139\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"139\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"167\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"167\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\"/>\n  <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"390\" y2=