t x=\"310\" y=\"269\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#059669\">13.0</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q76", "text": "A new island is formed by a volcanic eruption. Soil gradually develops on this new island, allowing grasses and other herbaceous plants to grow. These grasses and other herbaceous plants are gradually replaced by woody shrubs that are then replaced by trees. This change in community composition over time is best described as which of the following?", "options": ["Succession", "Reproductive isolation", "Speciation", "Geographic isolation"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q77", "text": "Which of the following is a type of bond in which electrons are shared?", "options": ["Covalent", "Ionic", "Hydrogen", "Electrostatic"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q78", "text": "Species X and species Y are in the same class, but not the same order. Species X and species Z are in the same order. Which phylogenetic tree best represents the relationship among these 3 species?", "options": ["Tree A", "Tree B", "Tree C", "Tree D"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 220\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <g transform=\"translate(10, 20)\">\n    <text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">A)</text>\n    <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"96\" y=\"44\" font-famil