line x1=\"60\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"96\" y=\"44\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">Z</text>\n    <text x=\"96\" y=\"94\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">Y</text>\n    <text x=\"96\" y=\"144\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\">X</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-5-q79", "text": "A scientist observes four female gray wolves, each from a different pack: Female 1 has the thickest fur; Female 2 produces the most pups that survive to reproduce; Female 3 has the most relatives in her pack; Female 4 survives the longest. Based on Darwin's theory of natural selection, which female has the highest biological fitness?", "options": ["Female 1", "Female 3", "Female 2", "Female 4"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-5-q80", "text": "Scientists often use the amino acid sequences of hemoglobin polypeptides to determine evolutionary relationships between organisms. The number of differences in the amino acid sequences of hemoglobin polypeptides between humans and vertebrates W, X, Y, and Z are shown in the table (W: 45, X: 32, Y: 67, Z: 125). Based on this data, which of these vertebrates is most closely related to humans?", "options": ["Vertebrate W", "Vertebrate Y", "Vertebrate X", "Vertebrate Z"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT — Test 5", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 450 230\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"450\" height=\"230\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#cbd5e1\" rx=\"6\"/>\n  <text x=\"225\" y=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\">Amino Acid Differences in Hemoglobin Polypeptides</text>\n  <rect x=\"50\" y=\"40\" width=\"350\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#f8