, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q14", "text": "How does carbon-12 (mass number 12, atomic number 6) compare to carbon-14?", "options": ["Carbon-12 has 8 more protons.", "Carbon-12 has 8 more neutrons.", "Carbon-12 has 2 fewer protons.", "Carbon-12 has 2 fewer neutrons."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q15", "text": "Biologists have linked the extinction of some amphibians to a pathogenic organism that infects their skin. During one stage of the pathogen's life cycle, it is motile and has a flagellum. The cell walls of the pathogen contain chitin, and mitochondria are present in the cells. How would biologists classify the organism, and why?", "options": ["As a fungus, because its cell walls contain chitin", "As a fungus, because it is pathogenic", "As an animal, because its cells have flagella", "As an animal, because it contains mitochondria"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q16", "text": "A peptide bond is formed between which of the following types of molecules?", "options": ["Amino acids", "Fatty acids", "Monosaccharides", "Nucleotides"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q17", "text": "Tiny single-celled algae called zooxanthellae live inside the bodies of reef-building corals. Through photosynthesis, zooxanthellae provide corals with carbohydrates, oxygen, and the proper pH to build coral skeletons. The corals provide the zooxanthellae with a protected environment, a source of carbon dioxide, and nutrients. What type of interaction is this?", "options": ["Commensalism", "Competition", "Mutualism", "Parasitism"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q18", "text": "Which of the following statements accurately compares rain to another substance in the table?", "options": ["Rain has a higher hydroxide ion concentration than ammonia.", "Rain has a higher hydroxide ion concentration than milk.", "Rain has a lower hydroxide ion concentration than vinegar.", "Rain has a lower hydroxide ion concentration than lye."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 380\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <style>\n    .th { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 15px; font-weight: bold; fill: #1A202C; }\n    .td { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; fill: #2D3748; }\n    .td-num { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; fill: #2D3748; text-anchor: end; }\n    .line { stroke: #CBD5E0; stroke-width: 1.2; }\n  </style>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"20\" width=\"390\" height=\"336\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"20\" width=\"390\" height=\"42\" fill=\"#E2E8F0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"62\" width=\"390\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#F7FAFC\"/>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"134\" width=\"390\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#F7FAFC\"/>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"206\" width=\"390\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#F7FAFC\"/>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"278\" width=\"390\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#F7FAFC\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"62\" class=\"line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"98\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"98\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"134\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"170\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"206\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"242\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"242\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"278\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"278\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"35\" y1=\"314\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"314\" class=\"line\"/>\n  <line x1=\"280\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"356\" class=\"line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"35\" y=\"20\" width=\"390\" height=\"336\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4A5568\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"47\" class=\"th\">Substance</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"47\" class=\"th\" text-anchor=\"end\">pH</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"86\" class=\"td\">Battery acid</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"86\" class=\"td-num\">1.0</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"122\" class=\"td\">Lemon juice</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"122\" class=\"td-num\">2.0</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"158\" class=\"td\">Vinegar</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"158\" class=\"td-num\">3.0</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"194\" class=\"td\" font-weight=\"bold\">Rain</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"194\" class=\"td-num\" font-weight=\"bold\">5.5</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"230\" class=\"td\">Milk</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"230\" class=\"td-num\">6.5</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"266\" class=\"td\">Sea water</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"266\" class=\"td-num\">8.5</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"302\" class=\"td\">Ammonia</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"302\" class=\"td-num\">11.5</text>\n  <text x=\"50\" y=\"338\" class=\"td\">Lye</text>\n  <text x=\"395\" y=\"338\" class=\"td-num\">13.0</text>\n</svg>\n"}, {"id": "act-6-q19", "text": "A base substitution mutation in a gene LEAST likely affects which characteristic?", "options": ["The structure of a protein", "The DNA's ability to replicate", "The sequence of amino acids", "The transcribed mRNA sequence"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q20", "text": "Which of the following is a type of bond in which electrons are shared?", "options": ["Covalent", "Hydrogen", "Ionic", "Electrostatic"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q21", "text": "Suppose a mating of 2 rabbits resulted in 1/4 of the offspring having black fur, 1/2 of the offspring having gray fur, and 1/4 of the offspring having white fur. The genotype of the black rabbits is BB. Which genotype and phenotype best describe both parental rabbits?", "options": ["BB, black", "Bb, gray", "bb, gray", "bb, white"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q22", "text": "The attraction between water molecules is an example of which of the following?", "options": ["Adhesion", "Cohesion", "Evaporation", "Transpiration"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q23", "text": "Which of the following is the best definition of biological evolution?", "options": ["The spontaneous appearance of life from nonliving matter after the formation of Earth", "The series of developmental changes an organism experiences throughout the course of its lifetime", "A change in the proportions of inherited traits within a population occurring over successive generations", "A means by which random chance blends the characteristics an organism inherits from its parents following fertilization"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q24", "text": "In the 1920s, biochemist Phoebus A. Levene proposed that DNA contains an equal amount of each nitrogen base and that the bases are organized in repeating clusters of 4. Which of the following statements best reflects Erwin Chargaff's 1947 correction of Levene's proposed DNA structure?", "options": ["DNA contains unequal amounts of each of adenine, cytosine, guanine, and thymine.", "DNA contains equal amounts of adenine and guanine, and unequal amounts of cytosine and thymine.", "DNA contains equal amounts of adenine and cytosine, and equal amounts of guanine and thymine.", "DNA contains equal amounts of adenine and thymine, and equal amounts of cytosine and guanine."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q25", "text": "Hydrothermal vents are found on the ocean floor where hot, mineral-rich water escapes from cracks in Earth's crust. Bacteria near the vents do not require sunlight. Instead, they get energy by oxidizing hydrogen sulfide. Clams, shrimp, and giant tube worms consume these bacteria. These animals, in turn, are consumed by larger animals. Removing which of the following components from a hydrothermal vent ecosystem would most likely impose the greatest limit on ecosystem productivity?", "options": ["Clams and shrimp", "Hydrogen sulfide", "Larger animals", "Sunlight"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q26", "text": "Occasionally during meiosis, nondisjunction occurs and a homologous pair of chromosomes fails to separate. Which of the following effects could nondisjunction have on the products of meiosis?", "options": ["One half of the gametes have 1 more chromosome than normal.", "All of the gametes have 1 more chromosome than normal.", "One quarter of the gametes have 1 less chromosome than normal.", "All of the gametes have 1 less chromosome than normal."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q27", "text": "Use the data in the graph to determine which relationship, if any, exists between the average annual rainfall and the number of mosquitoes.", "options": ["There is no relationship.", "There is a positive linear relationship.", "There is a negative linear relationship.", "There is an exponential relationship."], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": true, "visualNote": null, "visualSvg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 420\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n  <rect width=\"520\" height=\"420\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#1A202C\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"480,330 465,324 465,336\" fill=\"#1A202C\"/>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"40