: 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q47", "text": "Which of the following statements is the most complete and accurate description of meiosis?", "options": ["A single division of a haploid cell producing haploid gametes", "A single division of a diploid cell producing diploid gametes", "Two successive cell divisions producing haploid gametes", "Two successive cell divisions producing diploid gametes"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q48", "text": "Which of the following statements best describes a recessive allele?", "options": ["It produces the least common phenotype.", "Its phenotype is expressed in heterozygotes.", "Its phenotype is not expressed in heterozygotes.", "It produces the most common phenotype."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q49", "text": "Specialized cells of the pancreas produce insulin. Which of the following observations most strongly supports the conclusion that it is the IDX-1 gene that regulates insulin production?", "options": ["The IDX-1 gene is present in all body cells, including the pancreas.", "The IDX-1 gene is present in both liver and pancreas cells but is expressed only in liver cells.", "Products of the IDX-1 gene bind to DNA, regulating insulin gene transcription.", "Mutations of the IDX-1 gene have no effect on the regulation of insulin production."], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q50", "text": "Trait X is a dominant trait in humans. A man with Trait X, whose mother did not have Trait X, plans to have a child with a woman without Trait X. What is the percent chance that the child will inherit Trait X?", "options": ["0%", "25%", "50%", "100%"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6