, "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q54", "text": "Which of the following statements correctly identifies the charge of a subatomic particle and best describes the location of that particle in the atom?", "options": ["An electron is positive, and it is located outside the nucleus.", "An electron is negative, and it is located inside the nucleus.", "A proton has no charge, and it is located outside the nucleus.", "A neutron has no charge, and it is located inside the nucleus."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q55", "text": "Suppose a carbon dioxide molecule leaves a respiring muscle cell in the leg and is transported in the blood to the lungs. In what order does this carbon dioxide molecule most likely encounter these structures? (1: Heart, 2: Systemic vein, 3: Alveolar capillaries, 4: Pulmonary artery, 5: Capillaries near muscle cell)", "options": ["5, 2, 3, 1, 4", "5, 2, 1, 4, 3", "5, 4, 1, 2, 3", "5, 4, 3, 1, 2"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q56", "text": "When cells hydrolyze ATP, releasing energy, which of the following bonds in the ATP molecule is typically broken?", "options": ["The bond between 2 phosphate groups", "The bond between ribose and a phosphate group", "The bond between adenine and ribose", "The bond between adenine and a phosphate group"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": false, "visualNote": null}, {"id": "act-6-q57", "text": "Determine which of the following statements regarding food competition is most likely correct according to this aquatic food web.", "options": ["Krill compete with fish for carnivorous zooplankton.", "Sperm whales compete with elephant seals for krill.", "Krill compete with leopard seals for phytoplankton.", "Penguins compete with baleen whales for krill."], "answer": 3, "explanation": "", "source": "ACT 6", "hasVisual": t